/* Transcripts of the YouTube videos linked in the Speeches section, with short quotes and timestamp links. Retrieved or supplied November 8-9, 2026. Not proofread; watch the video to verify. */
(function (M) {
  M.captions = {"retrieved":"2026-11-09","byId":{"bottoms":{"videoId":"RUUu_rfqx9o","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"note":"This video is a press conference held the morning after the election, with questions from reporters. It is not the election-night speech.","excerpts":[{"text":"Yeah, I'm a governor for all of Georgia.","t":478}],"full":[[0,"Yeah. Y'all, it feels good to be a winner. And you all should all feel great because as I said last night, this win is for all of us. So, thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. And y'all can sit down. What a night. Um and I I'm still processing"],[32,"on 3 hours of sleep. So, maybe sometime next week I can fully absorb this moment. But I can just tell you all that um yesterday, and I said this last night, my my mom said God is going to show himself at his finest. And it was prophetic. We were expecting a very long night. Uh I was uh I had my AirPods in working on my speech. And um my husband kicked"],[63,"my leg. He was on the sofa next to me. I'm like, \"What is it?\" He said, \"They called the race.\" No, he said uh he said they called it. I said, \"Called what?\" He said, \"The race.\" I'm like, \"What?\" He said, \"You won.\" I'm like, \"What?\" No, it wasn't that I didn't expect to win. I just didn't know that it was going to happen that fast. [cheering] But it really speaks to the power of this campaign that has been fueled by"],[93,"you all in this room. From everybody who has worked on this campaign to all of the volunteers, to just the the community energy that has poured into this campaign and kept us going, it has all made a difference and our work has paid off. So, I just want to share a few stats with you. Hopefully I I I I'll have them right. Uh most votes"],[124,"for a governor in Georgia's history. The largest margin of win for a governor in 16 years. The biggest vote share for a Democrat in 40 years. [cheering] We flipped seven Trump counties. [cheering]"],[155,"And we won by nine points. SO, WE WE HAVE completed one leg of this journey. And the next leg will be for us to lead the state and to deliver on all the things that we have promised to do. And you'll often hear me speak of we because I'm a piece of the puzzle. I may be the face of it, but this really is about all"],[185,"of us. We heard the people loud and clear when they talked about challenges related to affordability, how they'll pay their rent, how they will access health care. We've heard people loud and clear when they've said that they can't get access in their communities. In fact, we're in a health care desert right here in this community. Uh we've heard people loud and clear when they said they need more access and expanded resources for mental health services."],[215,"We've heard our veterans loud and clear when they've said that uh the VA cuts have hurt them tremendously. We've heard our seniors loud and clear when they've said uh serving as a caregiver is draining them. We've heard people loud and clear on a woman's right to choose and make decisions about her own body. [applause] We've heard our teachers loud and clear when they have said they need more money, they need more resources, they"],[246,"need more support. And I can go through a list of 10 more things. So, what I can say to you uh is that we've already begun the work to begin laying out these priority areas and determine how during this transition period we quickly begin to address them and have a plan to deliver in January. Um I was very happy to have a conversation with Governor Kemp today and it was a very good conversation and his team is going to be available to us"],[278,"to help us uh with an orderly transition and a productive transition. So, I'm grateful uh for him extending that offer um and I I've told y'all this before. Uh we actually get along. Uh [laughter] Um so, it was it was a great call today. Uh but again, I just want to stop by and say thank you. Thank you. THANK YOU."],[311,"SO, BEFORE I I get to hug on y'all and love on y'all, I know there may be some questions. Am I out of order with what I'm doing? Okay. I'm getting We can take some questions from media here. I'll start off with you. Governor Bottoms, you won your race, but we also saw some historic wins for Democrats up and down the ballot. Can you just give your thoughts on the momentum behind Democrats this cycle? Well, we we were asking for whole ballot energy the entire campaign and it was"],[341,"uh it was why I kept repeating that. We wanted just what we got. We wanted wins up and down the ballot. We needed wins up and down the ballot. So, I'm very grateful that all of the constitutional offices [cheering] um uh have flipped. Uh we have taken the House and we have picked up several seats in the Senate. So, it was a good night."],[372,"Ma'am, you are from Atlanta and you won a historic race last night. What would you say to the young black girls who are living in communities like Atlanta who came to be what you are from now? Mhm. Ooh. Right up the street, just one block up, was Cascade Heights Hair Salon. The hair salon where my mother worked when she finished cosmetology school. I would ride my bus there after school."],[403,"And that salon was community. It was a place that people poured into me and made me believe that I could do anything I wanted to do. And for all of the girls and boys across Georgia, I hope that they know that all things are possible. And it is my sincere hope I've said it repeatedly. I want to be your favorite governor. And it is my sincere hope that the"],[433,"things that we do on behalf of all the children across this state will let will allow them to have a foundation to do whatever their heart desires. When I was writing my speech last night, we wrote some things in there about Jimmy Carter and how Jimmy Carter invested in education in this state. And he went on to create the Department of Education. Those things that have a lasting impact that have allowed me to stand here as governor-elect of Georgia."],[468,"Governor-elect, right here. Your acceptance speech, your message last night was one of inclusivity. What would you say to those Georgians who woke up this morning did not vote for you? Yeah, I'm a governor for all of Georgia. And the red clay of this state runs through my veins. And it is the reason why it even over this last week, I was in deeply red counties. I was in Dalton, Georgia the day before I'm I'm losing track of time. The day"],[498,"before the election, I believe is when we were in Dalton in Whitfield County, a place that Trump carried, I believe, by 70% plus. So, I want people to be clear from our rural communities to our urban cities that I'm thinking about them, and even if they did not support our campaign, I hope that they will know that I'm going to work on their behalf. WOO! CAN WE LOOK YEAH, COME HERE LIKE THAT."],[528,"UM UM YOU KNOW, THERE'S obviously there's the historic nature of your election. You're the first black woman elected governor in any state. We here in Georgia have had a black woman on the ballot for governor before. Right before your nomination, it was Stacey Abrams. Um she lost twice. Mhm. She won last night. Do you think it was timing? Do you think it was opponent? Do you think it was sentiment or policy? What do you think made the difference this year? You know, every election is an opportunity for us to learn and"],[558,"build, no matter who's on the ballot. And so, I I took what's worked well, I took what could have worked better, not just from those races, but all of the elections that we could gather data on, and I was uh talking with Vice President uh Harris on the way over here. Um and so, it is you know, we we all learn from each other. Um you'll have to ask the voters what made the difference this time around,"],[589,"but I what I know, and this is this is not about anybody else's campaign other than our campaign. I know that my team was the best campaign team that I could ever ask for. Um [cheering] I know that I had the best volunteers that any candidate can ask for. [cheering and applause] And it it all matters. It's it's it all"],[620,"matters. We build upon each other and there'll be somebody on the ballot uh in a year or two from now who will build upon our campaign in the same way I've had the opportunity to build upon others. Jonathan with our next question. Madam Governor-elect, you you mentioned that you're working on the transition into office. You've of course done this before when you took over as mayor. For folks at home, talk about what's involved in that and talk about in a little more detail, you know, the things that you're doing to hit the ground"],[650,"running as you said. Well, it's pretty intensive. One, you're looking at policy areas. That's the most important part. Um you're looking at, you know, how the all these things that that had been spoken about over the course of the campaign, then how do you deliver on those promises? What's the time frame? What's the staffing look like? It's it's um it's a complicated process, but certainly one that's necessary. I'm very grateful to have more time than I had when I transitioned"],[680,"into the mayor's office. I believe I had 3 weeks, maybe, uh for a transition because I went into a runoff. So, I'm grateful that this is the first week in November and not the first week in December. Mark Niesse with the AJC. Uh Governor-elect, you mentioned bottom of the can. Can you talk to us a little bit about how 2027 January, the legislative session. I know it's early, but some of the top two or three things that you hope lawmakers get together to help Georgians move forward, some of the policies that you campaigned upon. Yeah, so I just spoke with uh Leader"],[711,"Hugley on the way over here. I'll be giving Leader Jones a call as soon as I finish with you all and we're going to talk about alignment and how we can make sure that we are are as strong as we can be going into the legislative session and that we are aligned in in what we believe can get done this session and then of course we'll have discussions on that on that time frame. What can we do now? What will we have to push back until later? Uh but those conversations are already happening."],[742,"Ryan with our next question. Governor, you were you were outspent. There was so much money on the other side. Your team never gave up. Can you just talk about the fact of how you guys kept marching forward and how many people just took pride in that? Yeah. You know what, Ryan? And uh for for every $10 that someone dropped off at this desk at the door, it seemed as if my opponent was able to spend a million. And it was in There were some days that"],[774,"it really was a faith walk. And I've said it repeatedly, when we launched this campaign, God don't give vision without provision. And thankfully there are people in this room who believe that and stayed with us on that. And I didn't know where the resources would come from, quite frankly. I didn't know how we would do it, but I never wavered in believing that we could do it. And I at every turn I felt as if my faith were being tested."],[807,"And I would constantly have to remind myself that the same God who I believe placed in my heart the desire to run was the same God who stood with me every time a mailer came into my house, every time a TV ad went up, every time I I saw the numbers on the other side, uh it was you know, and I hope that I passed the faith test. Um and and and to the extent that I"],[837,"failed parts of the quiz, I stand here now as a believer. I can tell you that that um all things are possible. [applause] Governor Bottoms, your reaction to Governor Brian Kemp's decision that surprised many of you today not to call a special session to either strip your powers and or redistrict and dilute black voting power. I I was grateful, relieved, I exhaled."],[868,"Uh but, you know, I said all along I would deal with that when and if I had to. As my grandmother used to say, you don't worry unless you have to. So, of all the things I had to concern myself with the past week, that was not one that was going to keep me up at night. Um so, but I was grateful to hear that and I I've said this repeatedly, we are a state that's done really well in moderation. We don't do well, we don't do our best work, in my opinion, with extremes on one side or"],[898,"the other. And I believe that is that was an example that we're not going to jump off the cliff like so many other states have done. That this is really about um what's best for the people of Georgia. And as Governor Kemp shared with me, you know, it's worked well for many years and he didn't see a reason to do anything differently and I I appreciated that. And Alana, this is our final question. Um ma'am,"],[928,"um follow up to that question, uh did Governor Brian Kemp give you any clarity about what those budgetary issues might be that he signaled that there might be a special special session on uh ahead of the next one? No, he didn't and I I I won't speak for him. You know, he just mentioned that there were some priorities that he had. Um which I I respect, there's one governor at a time. So, as the person who will be the governor through the first part of January, that's certainly uh his prerogative to call a session to"],[960,"try and deal with some of those budgetary issues that he believes need to be dealt with in the special session. And again, what whatever that may be, we'll we'll see it when it happens. I'm just grateful they will not be touching the powers of the governor. Thank you for your time, Governor. Okay, and there's somebody over here with their hand up, too. And just thank you all to the elected officials here. Can you all wave your hands, too, please?"],[991,"Thank you. Thank you, council members. Thank you. Well, when I transitioned into the mayor's office, I had an amazing team that went through every single speech that I'd given over the course of the campaign. And they jotted down every commitment that I made, and they made"],[1023,"sure that I was held accountable to delivering. We worked out a plan as to how I would deliver on those commitments, and we tracked them weekly. And I'm very happy to say on the person led that effort, he's actually going to be leading some efforts on behalf of our transition. Specifically as it relates to Medicaid expansion, healthcare, the need for healthcare transcends party lines. It transcends geographical lines. It's an issue in our red counties in the same way it is in our blue and purple"],[1054,"counties. I truly believe that this is an issue we can get bipartisan support with. I know that there are many Republican leaders who support Medicaid expansion, and there are states led by Republicans that have Medicaid expansion. 40 states, we're are one of 10. And given that there are even more people expected to drop their um coverage under um the ACA, we know that the need for access to healthcare is going to be even greater. So, I'm I'm an"],[1087,"optimist. I think it will get done. Absolutely. My name is WBE. Talking about a policy, I'm just curious if you can just talk about your approach to the immigration policy you take on. Yeah, you know, Georgia is is supposed to be a welcoming state. It's who we claim to be as the cradle of the civil rights movement. We've always been open to a diverse uh group of people. Uh we"],[1117,"are now a majority-minority state. Um so, for us to to to not be respectful of our immigration policies and and humanely uh make sure that we're implementing policies that are humane and respectful really goes against who we are. So, you know, I don't see anything right now on the horizon, anything legislative, um that gives me pause with the Trump"],[1147,"administration, and then we will chart a course accordingly. Thank you. Okay. All right."]]},"hinojosa":{"videoId":"8TqBTWHLZlc","src":"captions-human","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"We did not end one era of single party rule just to usher in another.","t":824},{"text":"the people who write the biggest check to politicians in Austin","t":454}],"full":[[29,"Bigger in Texas including the shock. And this shocked the world tonight. With a Texas chip on our shoulder. It's possible"],[62,"-- It never -- bothered me that they doubted me. It bothered me that they doubted us. Hundreds and millions on attack ads written off over and over again. But Texas, my faith in you never wavered."],[97,"I have spoken to Governor Abbott. all to congratulate me. -- He extended a generous offer -- to assist with the transition. -- I want to thank -- him -- and -- his family for their years of service to this great state."],[135,"And now For you humble and grateful. All of the incredible grace and power of God. And of taxes. I am the daughter"],[166,"of the Rio Grande Valley. Where the people embody the work ethic and values of our great state."],[198,"-- Where no one -- would have imagined that one day, a little girl from the RGB. -- Would stand -- before you here as the next governor -- of the -- greatest state. But God had a plan. -- And -- the people of Texas"],[230,"had a plan too. It was a plan I did not know. I never set out to be a politician. I am a mom. I am a mom who loves her children, who believes in their teachers. And who -- believes in -- Texas public."],[287,"And when I saw my child's school under threat, I did what any mom would do. I fought back. I ran for the school board because I wanted my child and every Texas child to have the opportunity to succeed. From the school board to the House of Representatives. And now,"],[317,"with your extraordinary faith. And the trust of the people of Texas to the governor's. Here, only here, where no matter where you come from,"],[347,"no matter how humble your beginnings, your life -- can -- be bigger than your dreams. When we started this campaign a little over a year ago, -- I -- asked a simple question. -- Is Texas a state that is by and for the -- people? -- Or is -- this the billionaires' world and we just live here?"],[384,"Does Texas belong to the parents and their children? Or the billionaires trying to dismantle. Does Texas belong to the farmers and ranchers who Corporations trying to buy it up."],[415,"Does taxes belong to the working families who pay their Right. -- Or the wealthy and well-connected who play by -- different rules. Does Texas belong to the people who rise before the sun? Who worked two jobs. Help our homes to keep our hospitals running."],[446,"-- they've got into small businesses and -- big dreams. -- Or does it belong to -- the people who write the biggest check to politicians in Austin? Tonight, Texas, we answered. And we did not whisper."],[478,"Every billion I Belongs to us. The question we answered in McAllen and Corpus Christi. there. From the neighbor Austin to the wide open skies of West Texas."],[512,"Out to Big Ben. -- in our big cities where they -- tried to silence your voice with gerrymandered maps. And close polling sites only to see turnout like never. -- in small towns where people have been told their vote -- was already spoken for."],[542,"-- We entered in communities that politicians visit every 4 years -- to ask -- for -- your vote, only to forget about you as soon as they get to Austin. We answered in places that have been overlooked, underestimated and left behind for far too long. And we answered across party lines. It was always about whether the people of"],[574,"-- Texas ought to -- have a government that belongs to them. Highest bidder, not the biggest donor, not the most powerful lobbyist, you. -- And -- I wanna say something to the powerful people who have gotten very comfortable running this state."],[607,"have delivered a mandate for change. is -- With the politics of -- courage, not convenience. Progress will not be halted by partisanship, -- and -- Texas will bow down to no one."],[641,"Treating our public schools like they are for sale are over. Our tax dollars like your personal piggy bank are over. Days of writing one set of rules for working people -- and another for the wealthy -- and well-to do are over. of telling Texans to settle -- for -- less"],[671,"while only billionaires in boardrooms profit from the state we have all. Those days are over. -- By people with calloused -- hands and tired feet, -- by -- teachers and nurses. By oil field workers and truck drivers. By small business owners who put everything they had"],[702,"on the line. -- By -- parents who sacrificed so their children could have a better life. And those are the people who should come first in the state they built. -- They have -- labored and maintained an American dream through a long, hard night. My friends,"],[732,"it is morning now. Tomorrow our transition."],[763,"I will take the oath of office, ready to lead a government by the people and for the people. who donated the most. -- Not for the people who know -- the right people. But for every single Texan. Office does not belong -- to -- me."],[793,"It does not belong to my party. It belongs to you. This is our taxes, -- this is -- our government, and this is our one fight. And tonight we won."],[823,"Clear, -- we did not end one era of single party rule -- just to usher in another. The same national pundits and political class who ignored and then misunderstood this campaign will declare this a victory for Democrats. They continue to misunderstand. This victory is so much bigger."],[853,"in taxes. Victory for taxpayers who work too hard to see -- their money handed out to donors -- and special interests. We will end the era of no-bid contracts. and It is a victory for young people."],[884,"Across our state who possess unimaginable talents but have been left feeling so little hope. You will never have to choose between the state you -- love -- and -- a -- job that will pay your worth. have the economy that serves your ambitions, your dreams and your hard work. A government on your side, and the hope"],[914,"you deserve. The victory for teachers who will In case you have not heard, on day one, I will fire my."],[950,"Work tirelessly to repair the damage of the Texas voucher scam. In which our schools are sold for parts. A victory for the parents of Texas. We are taking our children's education back from a government that has failed them."],[982,"They will not be taken out of our control. They will not be shattered or suffocated. Being a parent is hard enough. Without carrying the burden of a government's failures. To the children of Texas. -- Your schools will -- not close. -- You will be invested in and you will -- grow up"],[1014,"-- in a Texas where you are lifted -- up every single -- day to -- reach your God-given potential. -- Tonight I make a solemn promise -- to every single Texan. Whether you voted for me or Greg Abbott or felt so betrayed by a broken politics that you did not vote"],[1044,"at all. Whether you're a Democrat, a Republican. Or neither. No matter where you live. No matter what your expectations of me are, no matter how accustomed you've become to corruption and incompetence, to experiencing government as something that is done to you. Not with you, or for you, or by you. Here's what Texas"],[1075,"said today. Loud and clear. Your government belongs to you. As your governor, I will never forget it. There will be no special set of rules for the wealthy and well connected. No looking the other way when someone in my own party does wrong. No excuses for corruption"],[1106,"-- because it comes from someone who shares -- my politics. Corruption does not become right when our side does it. Accountability does not stop at the doors of the governor's office, it begins there. The trust you have placed in me tonight is not a blank check. It is a sacred responsibility,"],[1136,"and I intend to earn it every single day. There will be times when we disagree. But I promise you this, I will always tell you the truth. And nothing but the truth. I will serve you and only you. I will listen when you disagree."],[1168,"I will admit when I am wrong, and I will never forget who sent me here. The power of this office does not belong to me, it belongs to you. And as excited I am by the history we've made tonight. -- I pray it does not compare -- to the future we build together."],[1203,"-- The nation will look at Texas and say -- we -- want -- something far more important than an election. They will look at Texas and say that faith in government has been restored. -- At Texas and -- see the power of a government that lifts every single person up and never punches down. -- We will build a government more -- honest,"],[1235,"more just, and worthy of the people Texas call home, and we will never forget the simple truth that brought us here tonight. Texas belongs to the people of Texas. No but think of my grandmother, Grandma Hinomosa. Who used to tell me. Note."],[1265,"Know your worth and fight to defend it. A lot of Latinas in Texas grew up hearing those same words. From their own mothers. Their own abuelas. This year we live them and we change this state and this win belongs to you and to them. -- And I need to thank some people here now -- who made this"],[1297,"-- all -- possible. Pablo, nobody has sacrificed more than you. You have You have been so supportive and gracious. And I am so proud of you. Even though neither you or Mateo ever asked for this."],[1329,"My fight comes from my deep love for the both of you and my desire to make this world safer and better for the both of you. You have been so understanding and encouraging, and I thank you both so much. To my husband John, -- Who I made promise to never run for -- office."],[1365,"You have been the rock who has held it all down and sacrificed and stood beside me in the hardest fights. This is not possible without you, and I love you. -- To my sister -- Sochi. You spent a year telling everyone who would listen that we would win."],[1401,"And with such certainty that it finally came true. I love you. You're the best sister a sister could ask for. Mom and dad, Cindy and Robert, my brothers and sisters and my entire family, thank you. Everything I"],[1431,"-- This day is -- because of you and I love all of you. To our next United States Senator James Teller. -- For years -- we believed there had to be a different and better way forward. It looks like we were right."],[1462,"Thank you and congratulations my friend. -- To Amy -- Friedman, my. You are an angel sent down from heaven to run this campaign."],[1495,"You believed in me and you believed in Texas. I will never forget all that you gave, all that you sacrificed to get us here. You led the best campaign team in the nation. A team that I hope gets some well-earned sleep tonight. To the people who showed up early for me and often who posted when I could still keep track of who was tagging me."],[1528,"Whether it was 10 times a day from Houston -- or DMs spreading my message to -- Texas newcomers. Who showed up at events when it was still only familiar faces. Who gave your labor and your love, and you took a leap of faith. Thank you. And to my hometown Brownsville."],[1572,"becomes, becomes of And God bless Texas."]]},"haaland":{"videoId":"XaWZvtvuU1I","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"I stand before you as the first Native American woman elected governor in US history.","t":367}],"full":[[0,"Oh, that was Thank you. Hello, New Mexico. [screaming] [cheering] Oh my goodness. Democrats have had an amazing night tonight. [cheering] So, I'm sure you had the popup on your phone that said Shared Brown won Ohio. Okay, everyone. I'm so happy happy to be here. S, thank you so much for that beautiful beautiful introduction. It's a great night to be new a new Mexican. Koati [screaming]"],[55,"Helpa Hanu. I want to thank my opponent Greg Hull for putting himself forward to lead our state and for running such a respectful campaign. [cheering] My ancestors came to the Rio Grande Valley in the late 1200s and this beautiful land has sustained all of us for generations. The home we all know. Mesaas, dotted desert, Yanos and agricultural fields. And just beyond this room, the rivers, mountains, valleys, and basalt flows from volcanoes long past. Tonight, our state proved that Democrats are entrusted to fight for our home, for New Mexico, not New America. [cheering]"],[119,"New Mexico's brightest days are ahead of us because I believe in a New Mexico that works for all New Mexicans. A New Mexico a New Mexico that embraces who we are, the care, the grit, and the heart that we have to lead the nation. To my running mate, Stephanie Garcia Richard, [cheering and applause] thank you for your partnership, your dedication to our state, and your hard work and commitment. It gives me endless pride to officially call you New Mexico's next lieutenant governor."],[165,"[cheering] [applause] To all the candidates up and down the ballot, congratulations. Thank you. Thank you for stepping up to serve our communities and working to build the New Mexico we all know is possible. To my to my amazing and incredible campaign staff, [screaming] [cheering] some who have been with me since we first launched on February 11th, 2025, 20 months ago. For some of you who don't want to get your calculators out and those who joined along the way, I thank you all for investing your heart and souls right alongside me. Thank you all so much [cheering]"],[228,"[applause] to the organizers and the awesome volunteers who knocked doors, made phone calls, talked to their neighbors, and believed in what we could accomplish together. This moment belongs to all of you [cheering] and to the people of New Mexico. Thank you for believing in me to lead our beautiful state for the next four years. [cheering] [cheering] We celebrate this moment right here along Route 66 on its centennial on Lagona PBLO land. [cheering] A huge a huge thanks to Maxine Velasquez and the whole team at Route 66 for making tonight possible. [cheering] And I'll just say it's always nice to see a woman in charge. [cheering]"],[294,"The historic Route 66 has connected our communities, brought people together, and opened doors of opportunity for generations of New Mexicans. Just off this mother road, my grandparents taught me the importance of hard work, our responsibility to care for our earth, and our duty to look out for our neighbors. This place, this land shaped who I am. I remember carrying water from the community spigot and playing outside from sunrise to sunset, spending time in my grandfather's cornfield, helping him irrigate. I remember watching my grandma bake bread and cook beans and chili. And just off this road, my grandmother was taken away to boarding school and along with my grandfather survived through a time where the federal government attempted to strip them of their languages, traditions, and identities."],[354,"Yet we are still here. [cheering] [applause and cheering] And tonight, in our nation's 250th year, I stand before you as the first Native American woman elected governor in US history. [cheering] [cheering] But tonight, [cheering] But tonight, tonight isn't only about history. Tonight isn't only about history. It's about our future. Right now, New Mexicans are working hard, doing everything they're supposed to do, and yet we still struggle to get ahead. Right now, there is a president in the White House who has enriched himself beyond comprehension while working his hardest to make New Mexicans sicker, poor, and hungrier."],[423,"But time and again, we have said no. It is our time. It's time. It's time for the single mother in Chaparel working two jobs, doing everything she can to keep food on the table to get ahead. It's time for the college student in Albuquerque who wants to build a future but has no hope because housing prices are through the roof to feel like he can graduate and build a prosperous future right here in New Mexico. [cheering] It's time for families in rural communities who travel hours to see a doctor unsure how they'll cover the cost to have affordable, accessible, high quality health care. [cheering] And it's time for union workers in New Mexico [cheering]"],[482,"to have better access to good paying jobs like helping build more affordable housing right here in our beautiful state. [cheering] And it's time to make it easier for every parent to give their children a better life that they have always hoped and dreamed of having. [cheering] And that's why I ran for governor. Because I believe in a New Mexico that works for all New Mexicans. Because I believe that no matter where you come from, how much money you have, or what challenges you faced, every New Mexican deserves the chance to thrive."],[529,"Every every New Mexican deserves a bright future. And tonight, New Mexicans have said decisively that they want the chance to build that future. [cheering] New Mexicans deserve a world-class education system. I will put reading coaches in classrooms and ensure our educators have the support they need to unlock every student's potential. Whether they choose college, the trades, or the military, New Mexicans know that CYFD must be fixed. and I will get to work on day one to ensure our kids receive the protection and care they deserve."],[579,"[cheering] New Mexicans need to feel safe in their neighborhoods. And that's why I'm committed to giving law enforcement the tools they need to get violent criminals and illegal drugs off of our streets so we can finally get ahead of this fentanel crisis and address crime at its source and get people the help they need. [cheering] New Mexicans are tired of having to travel hours outside of their communities just to access basic health care. I will create a path toward universal health care. [cheering]"],[623,"[cheering and applause] I will retain and recruit medical professionals and deploy mobile health care clinics so you can access the care you need not just when you're sick but to stay healthy. [cheering] New Mexicans deserve leaders who protect our water, our lands, and our precious natural resources. [cheering and applause] As governor, I will make sure industries don't come to New Mexico just to use us as a piggy bank while putting our future at risk."],[660,"New Mexicans deserve transparency. As new companies look to make New Mexico their home, I will demand accountability from every single industry. And because the affordability crisis leaves many New Mexicans wondering how we're going to pay for gas, buy groceries, or take care of our families, I will expand tax credits for working families and work to raise wages [cheering] so that more New Mexicans have money in their pockets at the end of the month."],[692,"Finally, when the federal government fails to live up to its obligations to our state, I will demand answers and fight for the funding that they have promised [cheering] because I've stood up to Donald Trump before and I'm ready to do it again. [cheering] [applause] [cheering] Right now, right now, while families across our state struggle to make ends meet, Donald Trump is gaming out a path of prosperity for him and his billionaire friends."],[731,"on January 1st. On January 1st, 2027, the day I'll officially take office, is the same month that 89,000 New Mexicans are projected to lose med their Medicaid coverage thanks to Trump's big ugly bill. He's cutting SNAP benefits and making families jump through endless hoops just to get basic health care. His actions threaten the very resources that thousands of New Mexicans rely on to survive. And he could care less."],[766,"So our work to combat Trump's cuts starts on day one. [cheering] Because no matter what comes out of Washington, we have a responsibility to take care of our people right here at home. Our state legislature is already leading the nation. Leading the nation by providing universal child care and early childhood education. [cheering] They have stood up for our state when our family SNAP benefits were at risk and they'll continue to fund higher education for our students."],[813,"[cheering] I am excited to work with all of you as we tackle our state's toughest challenges because to build a more equitable and prosperous New Mexico, we must work together. We need our teachers, nurses, firefighters, law enforcement officers, small business owners, [cheering] workers, and tribal and community leaders at the table. [cheering] And we need Democrats, Republicans, and independents alike to recognize that while we may disagree on how to solve certain problems, we have a shared responsibility to deliver solutions."],[861,"[cheering] So tonight, I want to speak directly to every New Mexican. To those who vote voted for me, thank you for your trust. [cheering] To those who did not, I want you to know that I am proud to be your governor, too. [cheering] I will listen to you. I will work with you. And I will never forget that serving every New Mexican is a governor's sacred responsibility. [cheering]"],[898,"[applause] Now, I know there are young folks watching tonight who may not know what their future holds. They may be growing up in small rural communities. They may be living on the resz. They may be watching from Espanola, Los Cuses, Ban, Hobs, or even Gallup. Some of them may be growing up in households where money is tight, where their parents work more than one job, or where they wonder what opportunities will actually be available to them when they grow up. I want every child watching to know, that your dreams matter, and that New Mexico is a place where you can build the life you want."],[945,"[cheering] [applause] Well said. Where you can build the life you want close to the communities that raised you. Here in New Mexico, we can do anything. [cheering] And I know this because I am living proof. [cheering] I spent years I spent years working on my sobriety. I raised a child in poverty as a single mom, registered voters in a res car along dirt roads and in dust storms to eventually serve in the halls of Congress and become the first Native American to serve as a US cabinet secretary. [cheering]"],[993,"[applause] And now I'm heading to the Roundhouse to serve as your next governor. [cheering] [applause] [cheering] As I've said, as I've said, my journey has never been mine alone. My parents raised me to work hard and to care. And I thank them both. To S, my sisters, and my brother. My wonderful extended family and former colleagues, I see the sacrifices you all have made for your families and our communities, and I am forever grateful."],[1048,"I stand here tonight because of the many generations who came before me, the family who looked out for me, and the New Mexicans who have always believed that a better New Mexico is possible. [cheering] [applause] I will fight for that fair shot at a New Mexico that believes in all of us. A New Mexico where anyone can grow up, build a family, find a good job, and be proud to call this beautiful state home."],[1081,"This [cheering] is the responsibility. This is the responsibility we all share. So tonight, this campaign ends and our real work begins. [cheering] We now turn our thousands of conversations into action, our promises into progress, and our shared vision into a better future for all New Mexicans. [cheering] With our grit, our creativity, our determination, and our willingness to look out for each other, I know we can accomplish anything together. And that's why I know New Mexico's brightest days are ahead of us."],[1129,"[cheering] God bless New Mexico. God bless our country. Thank you all so much. Dela, thank you. [cheering] You [applause] have to fill in All"]]},"acton":{"videoId":"ZRS2DGKD1_k","src":"captions-human","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"It is time for a statehouse that puts Ohioans first.","t":254}],"full":[[4,"Oh my goodness, oh my goodness. Oh Everyone, oh, it's, I am so honored to be here with all of you. I Oh, Ohio."],[35,"Oh. Yes. Oh, I am so incredibly honored that I have earned the trust of Ohioans to be. To be the next governor."],[69,"Oh my goodness. Eric and I want to thank all of you for your support, your love over the last 2.5 years, but especially over the last few weeks. It has meant the world to me and my family. This entire This"],[103,"This entire campaign has been a movement by and for the people. This win is for every Ohioan who has long longed for public servants again. Who solve problems instead of making them. And who do not mistake kindness for weakness."],[138,"Because of your hard work. Ohio has chosen unity and decency. Over division and hate. The healing begins today. We must never give up on one another."],[169,"This was a tough race. But the campaign is over. And, and I want to make something very clear to the people of Ohio. I will be a governor for all Ohioans. I am in this fight for all of us. My promise to Ohio,"],[199,"to those who voted for me, and those who did not, is that I will work with anyone and everyone, as I always have to make life better for Ohioans. I am incredibly honored and proud of the work I did with Governor Mike DeWine and his team. I look forward to continuing the work he has done"],[230,"around kids, around H2 Ohio, and so much more. I look forward to working with my colleagues in the legislature. On both sides of the aisle to ensure a very smooth transition. It is time for a statehouse that puts Ohioans first."],[260,"Not not special interests in corporations and billionaires. This is a moment for courage, courage. I will be asking for courage because we must fight for something bigger than ourselves. I have traveled this state for 2.5 years. We've listened deeply, and when I am governor, I will continue to do this."],[292,"I I have heard your stories, your hopes and dreams. It's truly an honor. People in this state are struggling. They're working harder than they ever have. There is no more breathing room. From the grocery and gas bills to the utilities, to childcare, to healthcare costs, Ohioans are doing everything right, but they just can't get ahead. I hear this story everywhere I go. It isn't about party for me,"],[323,"it never has been. It is about making life better for all of us. I know what it's like when people look the other way when you're struggling. As a child, I experienced abuse and neglect, and I could have never imagined going from homeless to being a doctor, let alone."],[359,"That I would be standing here, the next governor of Ohio. But I am here today because of the Ohioans who refuse to look the other way."],[390,"You have been refusing to look the other way. I'm here because of a couple who pulled me and my brother up on their front porch and fed us breakfast, knowing we were hungry. I am here because of every first responder, every teacher, every librarian, every. Mentor who lifted me up and gave me a fair shot. So this is what drives me, the belief that everyone, everyone deserves a chance"],[420,"to reach their full potential. This Love you too. I love you too. I am, oh God, it's it's unbelievable to look at you right now. Look at the face and the joy I've been seeing in crowds the last few weeks, watching you with one another. This win is for all of us, it is for all the scrappy kids."],[452,"the scrapping Who have been underestimated and overlooked or counted out. This is my promise to Ohio. No one will ever be unseen by me. Tonight my heart is full. I am filled with such gratitude and awe. There are so,"],[482,"there are so many people I wanna thank. First of all, to my running mate, David Pepper. I have to thank him so much for his relentless, and I do mean relentless, passion and commitment to making life better for Ohioans. How incredible it is to have a best friend and a partner"],[514,"to do this work with. To my scrappy, hardscrabble team. Who did the impossible every single day, and ran a campaign that led with passion, hope, integrity, dignity."],[544,"We started with nothing, not one penny, no more chest. And, and, and they believed in me and my mission. Thank you for giving everything to make life better in Ohio. That's you."],[574,"Someone seen it. Someone passed out, we're gonna hold for a minute."],[1382,"Oh, thanks everybody for your patience. She's doing well now, right? OK, good. So thank you to our, our first responders and everybody in the crowd. You guys did a great job. Thank you. Thank you very much. Well, where was I in I thanking people? All right, I want to thank every volunteer and supporter who gave your time and energy"],[1415,"and your heart to help us win. We did something different. We built a grassroots movement in this campaign. Thanks to Dan and Pat. And that proves something we've lost in politics. Relationships matter. Communities matter, our neighborhoods matter."],[1447,"To my brother Phil. You are the only person in the entire world who fully understands what we endured growing up together. And it was incredibly brave of you to share your story with the world. Thank you. From the bottom of my heart"],[1477,"for fighting for me. I love you so. I do. Thank you, Laura. To my family, um, Eric and the kids, all our friends who are here and there are so many here, I'm, I'm so grateful. I love you as my husband and I always say, forever and ever. Most importantly,"],[1507,"thank you, Ohio. None of this would have been possible without us linking arms and pushing back. Because of you, this stopped being just another campaign. It became a movement, and I am so grateful to every one of you, and I'm gonna be asking more of you yet. I have a deep belief in the resilience, the grit, and the kindness of our state,"],[1538,"and I wouldn't be here without it. Ohio, thank you for trusting. And believing in me. I trust and believe in you. It will take time to rebuild and create the Ohio we all dream of. We didn't get here overnight. In the days and years ahead, I'm going to be asking more of all of us. We will heal this thing that has been broken."],[1572,"And we will not give up on one another. Please don't give up on anyone in your life, even your friends. Your family, people who might have voted different, you, we've got to heal this thing. Together we are going to make life more affordable in Ohio. We are going to end the cost of corruption, and we're gonna build a state where all of us can get ahead."],[1606,"Now I will work with anyone to do this, but I want to be. I want to be very clear. I will be a relentless warrior for Ohio. To those who might want to exploit our state or to take us back into the hate, chaos, and vitriol, do not underestimate a scrappy kid from Youngstown."],[1644,"And Do not underestimate the people of Ohio. I love Ohio. It has always been and will always be Ohio. We are the heart of it all. For me, that is what this race has always been about, putting the heart back in the heart of it all."],[1674,"I want to build an Ohio that leads with integrity, with decency, where everyone can write their own story, where every kid gets a fair shot. I know I'm not the only one who saw a thing or two in their childhood in this room. None of us gets out of this thing unscathed. But our stories, Ohio's story, is one of resilience, of grit, of grace."],[1704,"And yes, of hope. Of hope Hope is what drives this movement because when we are in this together, we can build the Ohio of our dreams. Tonight, one journey is coming to an end, but a new chapter in Ohio is beginning. Tonight"],[1735,"Uh Tonight, let us celebrate. Tomorrow, let us get to work. Together, we are gonna build an Ohio where no matter where you were born,"],[1767,"you belong, you can build the life of your dreams and you can be whoever you want to be. Maybe even governor. Thank you Thank you for trusting and believing in me. I love you too."],[1800,"I will be with you, fighting alongside of you every step of the way. Thank you. Oh."]]},"becerra":{"videoId":"gCSPpr_4G5Y","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"after two years of chaos, corruption, and sky-high costs, we need that more than ever.","t":540}],"full":[[1,"To be standing in victory with all of you. [cheering] Now, I'm not going to sugarcoat it. These past 2 years have been tough. Higher prices, more wars, corruption and lawlessness, but we hung in there. Fought back. It felt like Mission Impossible. We knew it was mission necessary."],[31,"[cheering] And tonight, sisters and brothers, because of your tireless work, we can proudly utter the inspiring battle cry of our beloved and departed sister and warrior, the Dolores Huerta, \"Sí se puede.\" Yes, we can. Sí se puede. Yes, we can. YES, WE DID. WE FOUGHT. AND WE WON."],[61,"Thank you for making tonight's victory possible. Thank you for making history in this ELECTION FOR GOVERNOR. [cheering] AS CAROLINA SAID, THERE IS NO victory without you. And Carolina, there is no me without you. [applause] Together, we have made a life, a family,"],[92,"and now history. [cheering] Carolina, te amo sin fin. Beso, beso, right? [cheering] I'm not dumb. Come on."],[122,"But but honestly honestly though what value has history without a future? Being governor, don't get me wrong, is important. But my legacy was written the moment that Clarissa, Olivia, and Natalia entered this world. [cheering] Carolina and I have tried to do our part to place the future in fierce, resilient hands."],[152,"So I say to my three daughters, \"No pressure, girls. No pressure.\" [laughter] Ladies and gentlemen you have now entered THE BECERRA ERA. [cheering] BUT"],[183,"BUT BUT REALLY BUT really the Becerra era began in the 1950s when Manuel raised in Tijuana and Maria Teresa, who is here tonight from Guadalajara, Jalisco, Mexico [cheering] when the two of them came to California with $12 in their pockets. A construction worker and a clerical"],[213,"worker. Earned every dollar, saved every penny. They built their California dream. I watched and I learned. Thank you, Mom. Thank you, Dad [applause] for building the Becerra era. And and And here uh let me make something"],[243,"very crystal clear. I didn't run to make history. I ran to MAKE A DIFFERENCE. [cheering] FOR ANYONE AND EVERYONE WHO calls California home, whether you voted for me or not. For the next construction worker and clerical worker who want to buy their own home. For the first generation college student who is studying to follow Carolina's footsteps and become a doctor. [cheering] For the go-getter with a big idea, but"],[273,"little capital to start up the business. For the family with a medical emergency and a rent payment facing the prospect of homelessness. Remember, we are America's frontier model. A conveyor belt of invention, industriousness, AND GANAS. [cheering] DON'T LOOK IT UP. I'll tell you right now. [laughter] G A N A S, guts, grit, and game all"],[304,"wrapped in one. That's [cheering] ganas. [screaming] Every day, everywhere, Californians transform the seemingly impossible into the virtually unstoppable. And we do all of that as the most diverse place in America. [cheering] So, let me say to those in power who traffic in division and disinformation, there is no American greatness WITHOUT"],[335,"CALIFORNIA. [cheering] AND THERE IS NO CALIFORNIA without our diverse communities. [cheering] Diversity is not our shortcoming, it's our superpower. And it isn't our finish line, IT'S OUR BOTTOM LINE. [cheering] TO ALL OF THOSE OF YOU WHO HAVE FELT LEFT OUT, locked out, priced out, drowned out,"],[366,"down and out, even asked to drop out. Remember when I was in that race at the beginning of the primary? [cheering] I say to you, I say to you I say to each and every one of you this is your moment. [cheering] This victory is for you, the farm workers and firefighters, the teachers and tradesmen, small business owners and service workers, and my"],[397,"brothers and sisters from the [cheering] From the laborers, La Union in the house. I told you they were in the house. This victory is for you."],[428,"I also want to say thank you to my campaign team. As Catalina said, the best IN THE BUSINESS. [cheering] WE BUILT THIS PLANE MIDAIR and ran into a bit of turbulence in the primary from TIME TO TIME. BUT WE FLEW STRAIGHT and true. And man, DID WE LAND IT. [cheering] NOW, NOW THE REAL WORK BEGINS."],[459,"In 2 months I take the oath of office for the STATE'S HIGHEST OFFICE. [cheering] AND AND I WANT to be straight with you. California is exceptional but it is also far from perfect. We have a lot of work to do together. Despite all our fortune economic security is slipping out of reach for too many of our families."],[490,"Despite our shared values, not everyone who builds and harvests the California's success story gets to enjoy its fruit. As governor, my mission is straightforward, but not simple. Deliver a California we can afford. And defend a California we can't AFFORD TO LOSE. [cheering] AND HERE'S THE GOOD NEWS. CALIFORNIANS DON'T EXPECT a miracle from"],[520,"government. They just want a government that works. A government that can build things. A government that keeps our streets clean and schools safe. Basic services delivered on time and on budget. With leaders who are accountable and transparent, who can reach up without talking down. And after two years of chaos, corruption, and sky-high costs, we need that more than ever. Never in our lifetimes has so much of"],[551,"what we love been on the line. Our families, our safety, our freedom. Freedom to love, freedom to learn, freedom to unionize and earn a living wage. The right to see a doctor and the freedom to make your own decisions ABOUT YOUR BODY. [cheering] FREEDOM TO BREATHE CLEAN AIR, drink clean water, travel unpolluted"],[581,"coastlines. Freedom to walk the streets without fear of gun violence OR ICE MERCENARIES. [cheering] AND FREEDOM TONIGHT to hold A FREE ELECTION. [cheering] CUZ ZIP IT, THIS IS CALIFORNIA. WHERE NO PROBLEM is too big to solve, and no person is too small to matter. The California dream is universal, it's"],[613,"non-negotiable, and yes, it is undeportable. [cheering] Tonight, I have a message for all those who have been made to feel afraid. There's a new SHERIFF IN TOWN. [cheering] AND HE'S GOT A LAW DEGREE AND A UNION CARD. [cheering]"],[643,"IF ANYONE WANTS TO COME AFTER California or any one Californian, they better be ready FOR A FIGHT. [cheering] WRITE THE LOTUS. We can't be bought, we can't be bullied, and we will never, ever back down from a fight worth fighting. [screaming] And our people, our values, and our resources are always worth fighting for."],[675,"Brothers and sisters, THIS IS CALIFORNIA'S MOMENT. TONIGHT, all across the country, in blue states and red states and all over the places in between, voters are choosing hope and repair over DIVISION AND DESPAIR. [cheering] AFTER TWO exhausting years of red flags, America's following California's blue BEACON OF LIGHT."],[708,"[applause] SO, ARE WE READY, CALIFORNIA? [cheering and applause] IT'S TIME FOR CALIFORNIA to adopt the Muhammad Ali mentality. If our minds can't conceive it, and our hearts can't believe it, then we CAN ACHIEVE IT. [cheering] AND IF I were a little younger, I'd do the shuffle and roll right there at the same time. So, I ask you, California, are you READY TO LEAD? ARE YOU READY TO ACHIEVE?"],[739,"[cheering] THEN BROTHERS and sisters, here in California, we're going to get to work. Thank you all very much. Thank [cheering] you. God bless this great state and our great nation. THANK YOU."],[808,"OH, YEAH. RIGHT."],[980,"MHM."]]},"crowley":{"videoId":"xgXbobtgdcY","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"In a state this close, nobody gets to govern alone.","t":654}],"full":[[16,"Wow. Thank you. [cheering] Thank you. Wisconsin. Thank you so much. You know, to my wife Erica."],[47,"Thank y'all. Thank you so much. You know, I first have to say thank you to my wife [cheering] It's been her strength, her resilience that have propelled me and this campaign through our hardest days. And I am so blessed to have you by my side. And I can't wait for Wisconsin to get to know"],[78,"you as their next first lady. to to our three beautiful daughters, Alyssa, Ava, Autumn, we call them the A squad, y'all. And I want to let them know that nothing in my life makes me more proud of being their dad."],[110,"Thank you for believing in me as much as I believe in you. And I hope that they see tonight that no matter the setbacks that life throws you, if you work hard and be kind, anything is possible. I love you guys. And I would not be here, I would not be the man I am today if it was not for my parents. And so I want to say thank you to my father David, my stepmother Beth"],[143,"for their unwavering love and support. But I also want to give a special thank you to my mother Valerie. It was her determination and grace that made it life so much more possible. And while I wish she was here tonight, I know that she is proud of what we've been able to build together, y'all."],[173,"And to the incredible Sarah Galooski, our next lieutenant governor, YOU KNOW, I hit the jackpot with this one on the campaign, and I know the same will be true while we're governing. And I can't wait to get to work with you for the people of this great state. and to the man that I look up to personally and professionally, our great Governor Tony Ivers."],[204,"For eight years, you and your team fought every single day to make life better for our friends and for our neighbors. Governor, I am proud to call you my friend, honored to have had your support in my campaign, and I will build on what you have been doing and have done to keep moving the great state of Wisconsin forward. And so, thank you to not just our great governor, but also to Kathy Ivers for all that you have done and sacrifice for the great people of this state. [cheering]"],[238,"This wind, this win belongs to the volunteers who knock doors in the rain and the cold. To the union members who spent their precious time walking their own neighborhoods. To the staff that gave their campaign a year of their lives. and to everyone here and beyond who chipped in five bucks because they believed. And I especially want to thank my campaign manager, Garen Randolph,"],[270,"who is the loyal and steady hand guiding this campaign from the very beginning. But this win also belongs to Milwaukee, the city that raised me. [cheering] It belongs to Milwaukee, the city that raised me, and to every corner of this state that showed up tonight. And to everyone, to everyone who started this year"],[301,"backing someone else and finished it on our team, thank you. We are stronger because you are here. Thank you. And I would be remiss if I did not say thank you to the clerks and to the pole workers who work before sunrise until the last ballot was counted. Thank you for your hard work. Thank you for participating in our democracy. A few minutes ago, I had the opportunity"],[332,"to talk to Congressman Tom Tiffany and I thanked him for a hardfought race and for his service. But despite our differences, I've never doubted that he loves the state that we both call home. Finally, to the people of Wisconsin, tonight is for all of you. This is for all of you. And you know, I always say that every day is a good day, but Wisconsin, this"],[363,"is a very good day. This is a very good day. [cheering] Because of bo because of you, a boy who grew up facing eviction will now live in the governor's residence. Tonight, Wisconsin made history and being your next governor is humbling in its own right."],[394,"I don't take any of this lightly and I know exactly the shoulders that I stand on and I want to say thank you for placing your faith in me. That's ultimately what voting is. A tremendous act of faith. Not faith in one person or a party, but faith in the idea that elections matter. That the right leadership can make a difference in people's lives. Because when you're sitting around the kitchen table at night having to decide which of"],[424,"your bills would go past due that month or when your kid is sick and your or a parent needs caretaking but your job doesn't afford to leave for those that you love. When a family moves off a farm not because they want to leave but because they don't see a future in stain. You don't really care about the letter that's behind the candidate's name. You just want to know that those who empower that they see you"],[454,"and that they're doing everything in their power to actually deliver. And I just want you to know that is exactly what we're going to do for the people of the great state of Wisconsin, y'all. But I want to be very clear when I say we, I don't just mean Democrats. I mean, we as public servants of both parties whom have been elected to work together on your behalf. I ran to be a governor for all of us. And tonight,"],[485,"that includes everyone who didn't vote for me. I want you to know that I'm going to listen to you, that I'm going to work for you, and I hope to earn your trust the best way that I know how, and that's by showing up and by delivering results. I stand here tonight. I stand here tonight with deep gratitude, believing more than ever that what unites us as Wisconsinites is so much"],[516,"bigger than what divides us. We love our families and our communities, no matter how big or how small. We believe in hard work and that our kids tomorrow can be brighter than our today. and whatever else we argue about, I do believe that we will always bleed green and gold. And thanks to the Milwaukee Brewers, each and every one of us in this room and beyond are world champions. [cheering]"],[547,"It isn't partisan to want good public schools where every child is safe and loved and on a path of success. Republican voters are worried about what they pay for healthcare. And there are Democratic voters who want us to be sound stewards of their tax dollars. at the gas pump or at the checkout line. No matter asks whether you're a Democrat or a Republican, those bills, they hit all of us the same. And you know what? I"],[579,"GET IT. MY DAD, HE WAS A IBW Master electrician. My mother, she was a Jane of all trades. And yet, growing up, there were nights where I didn't know if there would be food on the table. Days where I couldn't go or be able to get to go to school because I couldn't afford the bus fair. I grew up in one of those families. not knowing if there will be a roof over your head or if the next doctor's bill will wipe away your finances, hoping that someone in charge would give"],[610,"families like ours a fighting chance. So, to all of those families who are watching tonight, I see you. I hear you. I was you. And now I'm going to fight for you each and every single day. [cheering] Now, there's going to be folks who are going to look at today's results, and they're going to see a closely"],[641,"divided state. They'll shade the map red and blue, and tell you one color came out on top. But I see something different, y'all. Wisconsin isn't a red state or a blue state. We never have been. In a in a state this close, nobody gets to govern alone. When majorities are narrow, there's no room for show votes or shouting matches. There's no time to waste on culture wars that make for great Instagram clips or lousy"],[672,"government. There's only room for the work, fixing the damn roads, funding the schools, keeping our communities safe, and bringing down your monthly bills. [cheering] In a state like ours, the voters keep everybody honest. And tonight, they told all of us in both parties, we are sending you to Madison to get something done. Now go do it."],[702,"And I just want to say to Wisconsin, message received. So to every member of the legislature, Democrat or Republican, my door is always open. Starting tomorrow morning, I'm going to sit down with anyone who is serious about lowering costs for our working families. We won't agree on everything, but we don't have to agree on everything in order to agree on something. And"],[732,"there's A WHOLE LOT OF something that needs to be done and waiting to be done. And this is why we have to get it done. And so I remain I remain optimist optimistic that tonight we will see Democratic majorities. And for the first time since 2010, Wisconsin voters will trust us to lead. Close margins will mean we earn that trust every day. But we do it by"],[763,"governing the whole state. But still, the people of Wisconsin elected me as their governor. It's it is my responsibility to offer my vision where we are headed and to provide the leadership to bring us together to get it done. So, here's the work that I intend to do on your behalf."],[794,"We're going to lower costs for housing, for utilities, and for child care. We're going to bring real property tax relief. We're going to provide health care that you can that is both accessible and affordable, but with real options, good schools funded without a referendum every other year. [cheering] A government that is open, accountable, and transparent. And guess what? None of these are Democratic or Republican"],[825,"ideas. These are Wisconsin ideas, y'all. And for those of us who are headed to Madison in January, our job is to get it done. And many of you know that our state's motto is just one word. It's right here on our flag. Y'all know what that is? Forward. That word doesn't just belong to one party or one election. It belongs to the dairy farmer in"],[856,"Marathon County and the nurse finish finishing a double shift right here in Milwaukee. It belongs to our elderly ne elderly neighbors who've gotten us to this place and even every young person was in this room who inherit what we build next. It belongs to the young kid somewhere in our state facing eviction and struggling. Who knows he or she may one day become governor. Tomorrow, tomorrow the signs will come down. The"],[888,"ads will finally stop and we will go back to being what we always once were, neighbors. So, let's show the country how it's done in a world that is all too divided. Let's buck the trend in true Wisconsin fashion, y'all. Let's be the state where elections make us better, not bitter. Where we stop asking where an idea came from and"],[918,"instead ask where will it take us. The great Vince Lombardi once said, \"People who work together will win.\" Whether it be against complex football defenses or the problems of modern society, people who work together will win. Not Democrats, not Republicans, but people, y'all. And I learned that people beats money power each and every single day. AND SO TO MY"],[949,"FELLOW WISCONSINITES, WE ARE NOT A RED STATE. WE ARE NOT A BLUE STATE. WE ARE NOT DEFINED BY RURAL AND URBAN. WE ARE ONE PEOPLE, ONE WISCONSIN. AND TONIGHT, WE CHOOSE TO MOVE FORWARD TOGETHER, Y'ALL. THANK YOU, WISCONSIN. GOD BLESS YOU ALL. AND LET'S get to work. Thank you. David Crowley's acceptance."]]},"ford":{"videoId":"_zAesbDnTRo","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"note":"This is a 63-second clip, not the whole speech.","excerpts":[{"text":"Whether Nevadans, not billionaires, not special interests, not politicians decide what happens in the Silver State.","t":29}],"full":[[0,"This campaign didn't happen by accident. It happened because of faith. Because of family. Because of hard work. And because the people of Nevada decided that our best days are still ahead of us. You see, this election was never about one party beating another. It wasn't. It was about whether working people in Nevada have a government that works for them. Whether Nevadans, not billionaires, not"],[31,"special interests, not politicians decide what happens in the Silver State. And Nevada is answering right now."]]},"klobuchar":{"videoId":"n6gHRJiIZR0","src":"captions-human","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"I am committed as ever to moving our state forward, not moving our state to the left or to the right","t":56}],"full":[[0,"All right, well, thank you, everyone, uh, for being here and thank you for joining us today. I know that people were most likely, uh, up quite late last night. I know I was, um, and it was obviously a big night, uh, both nationally and in Minnesota, um, and the country spoke out. With nearly one voice from South Carolina and Texas to Ohio and Kansas, from"],[30,"small towns to the suburbs, uh, to the metropolitan areas, and people are obviously sick and tired of the cost and the chaos and the corruption coming out of this administration in Washington DC. But we're here in Minnesota and my job is to focus on what's before us in Minnesota. I am committed as ever to moving our state forward,"],[60,"not moving our state to the left or to the right, but moving our state forward. Many Minnesotans voted for me and some didn't, and as we prepare for my administration, I want every Minnesotan to know this whether or not I got your vote, I will do my best for you. I will work my heart out for you. Nobody will work harder."],[91,"I am relentlessly focused on bringing people with us to transform Minnesota and transform our state government to match your drive and ambition. Last night I spoke about the campaign that we ran. It was a campaign built on substance instead of political punch lines. One columnist today said it was flawless, which I truly appreciated."],[122,"I guess he wasn't behind the scenes at every moment, but we really did our best to put out our best for the people. But for me there is no time to look in the rearview mirror back at everything about that campaign. And the ads and everything. My focus starting this morning is to move our state forward. That's what I will do as your governor with my lieutenant governor Ben Shire. You see how coordinated we are already on the"],[153,"first day with his matching tie with my suit. So, uh, we are gonna work together flawlessly. Uh, we, uh, believe, uh, that we must have a vision which I've laid out during this campaign. And that we must have goals, uh, which we will lay out and that we also must be accountable to the people of this state. So here we go, number one, transforming state government we're going to rebuild trust,"],[184,"speed up government, and work for you. That means rooting out the waste, fraud, and abuse and cutting through the red tape. It begins with the top to bottom audit of our state government starting on day one. There will be zero tolerance for fraud in my administration. We will work to every day stop fraud before it starts. How? By vetting grants and contracts before funds are awarded and screening providers before the money goes out the door."],[217,"We'll have in-person inspections and unannounced visits, and if you're caught trying to rip off Minnesota taxpayers, there will be serious consequences. We will strengthen criminal penalties and send those who commit fraud to jail. We will also make government more effective. Your tax dollars should get you good customer service. We'll cut through the red tape that slows"],[248,"everything down while streamlining and consolidating services. For one, permitting needs to become more efficient. You should be able to track applications on routine requests of our government just like you track a package and if it's not decided or processed by a certain date, you should get your money back if Domino's can do that we can do it too. Here's the bottom line if something works or is working, we will keep it."],[278,"If it's broken, we will fix it or get rid of it. Number 2, expanding our economy with a growth agenda. Minnesota built this nation. We do big things. We brought the world everything from the pacemaker to the Post-it note, but we cannot rest on our laurels. We must continue to be a state that makes stuff, that invents things, that exports. To the world for that to happen, we must make it easier to do business and create good jobs in Minnesota"],[311,"and give Minnesotans the skills and the pathways that they need to get those jobs. We have a strong foundation and we should never forget that with 18 Fortune 500 companies and 500 small businesses, but we cannot rest on our laurels. I will be a partner to the innovators in our state. I will be a partner to the workers in our state. I will be a partner to the business leaders in our state to streamline processes so it doesn't take months"],[341,"or a degree in rocket science to start a business, build and expand a business, and bring good paying jobs to our state, except maybe for the aerospace industry that is developing in our state. You might want a rocket degree. I will also expand Minnesota's workforce because any Minnesotan should be willing to, who's willing to work, should be able to have a path forward, a path to success that starts,"],[371,"of course, with our K through 12 schools. I'm very serious about getting student achievement up and screen time in the classrooms down. And when it comes to job training, we have this moment in time as we see AI coming our way, which of course needs guardrails on the federal and state basis, but we have this moment to look at our workforce needs. There are a whole bunch of AI proof jobs out there, jobs that are open right now, whether it's in the health care field,"],[401,"whether it is in the trades. And Ben and I are committed to adding 10,000 more apprenticeships. That's doubling the apprenticeships in our state in a vast number of areas because we know that is a key for many young people or even workers that are leaving jobs and going into new jobs. It gives them that opportunity to get that leg up, to get that job. I will work with colleges, businesses, and with the labor unions to expand pipelines to jobs in education,"],[435,"health care, public safety, and emerging industries. Our future is up to us, and I truly believe we can get to a better place together. Number 3, taking real steps to make life more affordable. We will take action to address the high costs Minnesotans are facing, including healthcare, housing, and childcare. On health care, I've outlined my plan. It is right there on our website"],[466,"to bring down the cost of premiums by blocking unfair insurance rate hikes, extending reinsurance, and creating a state tax credit if the federal. Government won't act, although those chances have improved after last night when it comes to the very important tax credit, given that 8 million people have been tossed off their healthcare nationally since the president came into office. I will build on my years of fighting and beating Big Pharma"],[500,"to lower prescription drug prices by expanding bulk purchasing of drugs. Housing should be more affordable. That's our goal. We will work with the private sector to build 100,000 more homes, from apartments to single family houses. The road to housing bill that just passed the Congress this last year is going to be very helpful in paving that way, and I know where the money is buried over there. And I also know, uh,"],[530,"the provisions in that bill since I wrote part of it. We must build houses faster, and that means permitting needs to be faster as well. Clear timelines, quicker decisions, more homes. Finally, I believe that Minnesota families deserve child care that is safe, affordable, and high quality. We will support innovative child care models, build new facilities, expand the child care workforce, streamline the funding that's there now for scholarships and other things."],[564,"Many more kids can be helped, and this is another place to cut red tape. That's my vision for our state's future. I've really kept to the same vision from the minute I announced this campaign, I'll be it a short one, to the end. The election is now behind us and it's time to get to work. So today is day one of my transition and I'm glad to share some of the details of that. Uh, first of all,"],[594,"um, my well respected, uh, friend and former deputy way back at the county attorney's office, Cindy Justin is chairing our transition team. She is a former court of appeals judge. And she served as commissioner of human services during the Dayton administration and has a very good understanding of some of these agencies that need to be fixed. As I mentioned, she was also one of my top deputies in the Hennepin County Attorney's Office."],[628,"When I came into that office, I made a number of changes, and I know she was a change maker that helped me to do that. She also worked with then Chief of Staff Tina Smith on Governor Dayton's first transition. So she will lead our transition team to put our administration in position to begin delivering for Minnesotans right away with accountability and with integrity. Cindy will be joined by many others."],[658,"These are volunteers. These are not necessarily people that will serve in the administration, but they are committed to helping me build the team, the new team that we need in place. They include as our co-chairs, Doug Baker, the. Former chair and CEO of Ecolab who has served on the executive committees of the Greater MSP Partnership and Minnesota Business Partnership, Miguel Pozzo, who has 30 years of experience as a trial attorney,"],[691,"corporate counsel, and compliance professional, he was also head of the National Hispanic Bar Association. And he has served for me on a number of committees, judicial selection committees for federal judges, so I'm well acquainted with his work. Justin Bowen right over there, um, who has been a close adviser to me for years and actually headed up my presidential campaign. Rose Sullivan, who started with me way back when she was just out of Gueststatuss,"],[723,"was in my office for over 12 years as our healthcare LA and then became my legislative director and then my chief of staff in Washington, and I'm very fortunate, uh, that, uh, she and her husband Tom, who was Blincoln's top adviser, have moved back to Minnesota with their four children. Uh, she has those 10 years of experience with me, but she also was the associate director for health programs at the White House Office of Management and Budget and worked directly,"],[757,"uh, with then commissioner Secretary Becerra and who is now the governor of California as of today, um, and has a lot of healthcare experience as well, Lee Sheehy. is joining us as well. He chaired Governor Dayton's judicial selection commission and also served as my chief of staff. Sam Clark. He is a senior attorney in the Ramsey County Attorney's Office, and he previously served as my state director"],[788,"and my counsel in the US Senate. Kim Norton, the mayor of Rochester and a former representative, as many of you know her, who served in the Minnesota House for 10 years, Melvin Carter, who served as Saint Paul mayor and city council member and as director of the Minnesota Office of Early Learning and executive director of the. Minnesota Children's Cabinet. Tony Surdich, a longtime friend, president and CEO of the Northland Foundation,"],[818,"currently, and a former Minnesota House majority leader who represented the Iron Range for a decade, Scott Badness, president of the Minnesota Professional Firefighters Association. Representing more than 2000 firefighters, paramedics, and dispatchers across the state, Dan McConnell, president of the Minnesota Building and Construction Trades Council, representing more than 70,000 skilled construction workers statewide, you all know what a big emphasis I have on"],[849,"infrastructure for my time in the Senate and here, as well as the emphasis that I'm going to put on clearing out red tape to make it easier to build projects. Mike Kohang, dean of the Morrison Family College of Health at the University of Saint Thomas, Gary Wordish, president of the Minnesota Farmers Union and a member of the National Farmers Union Board of Directors. Together these leaders from across our state will work"],[880,"with me on a volunteer basis to identify and recruit Minnesotans for my administration. Additional leaders on the transition will be announced in the coming weeks. There are 61 days before my administration begins. Being governor will be a marathon, but this will be a sprint. Every single day will count. We will need a new team,"],[910,"and we will be filling roles across state government and we want fresh voices and new ideas to transform our government and we want ideas from existing employees, uh, once I get there, uh, that I think are very important for those that work in state government about how we can make each agency work better. People are welcome to express interest on our new transition website. We had to work really hard on it this morning."],[942,"Our new transition website, which launched today at gov Klobuchar.com. We are asking people to put their names in if they are interested in these positions. My administration is going to be committed to carrying out this vision to improve the lives of Minnesota. Ben and I are dedicated to uniting Minnesota, to bringing our state together and delivering real results that you can see and feel"],[974,"in your life. And just as I have as your United States senator, I pledge to work every single day, not just for the people who voted for me yesterday, as much as I appreciate that, but for all Minnesotans. Thank you. Governor-elect. Governor Governor-elect, yeah, that's right. Or -- whatever you -- want. Amy is fine, uh, Senator, Governor-elect, uh, congratulations first of all. How is this top to bottom audit of state government"],[1006,"going to look on day one? The commissioners you appoint, will they be expected to undertake that effort? So as governor, as I have pledged from the first day, uh, when I decided to run for this office, I will launch a top to bottom audit of our state government to make sure it is actually delivering and that is both, let's make clear here to root out the fraud, yes, but also to figure out at a time of budget constraint"],[1036,"how we can make the state government work better and as I said, we will. Fix what isn't working or get rid of it and we will certainly keep what is working. So how does this work and great question. I will appoint an independent senior leader to conduct the audit of every agency across state government with a focus on rooting out waste fraud and abuse. The auditor will work with the new inspector general. That law that was passed,"],[1067,"I was supported last year has its own timeline. So I want to make sure that we don't waste any time and we get the, the audit started right now. Then when the inspector general starts, when that office is brought up, uh, we will then be working with that office. um, and all I want is not to have more overlapping of authority and more overlapping of work that has to be done. So that clearly is going to have to be coordinated."],[1097,"The auditor will work with this new inspector general and Minnesota management and budget to conduct the audit. So there may be things that my office is working on with government programs and figuring out what works while at the same time we're rooting out the fraud and doing that piece of it that eventually will be moved over to the inspector general. Um, they will also coordinate with the legislative auditor. I'm well aware that we have 3 things going here."],[1127,"And use previous findings from audits let me say that again previous findings from audits that's for the legislative auditor to hear as well as everyone else, um, and make sure that those are implemented and then again making sure that we work with the legislative auditor to get their ideas, um, and figure out what. We can do to make state government better. I always looking back to some of the things I saw in the federal government or when I was county attorney,"],[1157,"uh, when we would have a, let's say a horrific murder or something go wrong, we would do something that was like a postmortem in the county where every single. Agency involved would look at what they did wrong and come to grips with how did this happen? Could we have caught something earlier? We wanna be very open to hearing from employees and change the culture, uh, so that we know not it's whistleblowers, yes, but it's also how can we fix things"],[1187,"and figure it out, uh, from the governor's office down and I'm gonna finish. I'm not quite done with this because it's so important. I'm also going to direct the agencies to create a clear process for reporting fraud, and we will work with whistleblowers as I noted, and I will direct agencies to develop action plans to immediately address findings and recommendations by the legislative auditor. And I also have another commitment on the, the front of the legislative auditor that my office"],[1218,"will be meeting regularly with the legislative auditor. Governor-elect, how do you see this effort coordinating then? How do you see this effort coordinating then and also your desire to work with business with now a democratic legislature which might be very progressive and these are some more moderate concepts. How do you see that colliding or coordinating? Well, um, first of all, uh, this is going to be very important to me. I will note that while I may have talked to a lot of US senators over the last."],[1248,"48 hours and a lot of incoming US senators, um, some of whom you saw on TV all last night. The most 4 important calls I had today were with Erin Murphy, the new majority leader, Zach Stevenson, uh, the incoming Speaker of the House, I believe this depends on their caucus votes, um, but I also spoke with Mark Johnson on the Republican side in the state Senate. I spoke to Harry Niska"],[1279,"on the House side and of course, I spoke to Speaker Dameth last night and I really appreciated how gracious she was. This is gonna be very important to me to implement the work uh that I need to get done. And while, yes, uh, there are of course progressives on the Democratic side, there were also a number of moderates that got elected last night like Jim DeMay and Jen Fox, um. Chris Swanson, Mark Legbold, um,"],[1309,"I think you're going to see, as you do and I see every day in my own caucus in the US Senate, you're going to see people with different views. And the most important thing to me is that people know where I am coming from and the fact that I have been consistent from the beginning, including last night, we're in front of the entire celebration, which was an ongoing and never ending celebration. Uh, for the Democratic Party nationally in the DFL, I actually said"],[1340,"spoiler alert, you're not gonna like everything I do because I think it's really important for people to understand that we are in agreement on the purpose here. The purpose is to make the government work and I talked to all four leaders about this, and they are all committed. To this, make the government work, the state of Minnesota's government work better, and that means cutting through the red tape. That means rooting out the fraud, and we have agreements on that. We have agreements on improving people's lives."],[1370,"There may be differences here and there on the policies on how to bring down costs, but there is agreement that that should be a. Purpose of the Minnesota state government we have agreements that we should be keeping people safe, public safety, so I am actually quite excited, uh, to work, uh, with these leaders and, um, they have, you know, all have vast experience with the state government and I'm also excited to be working with the new members that are coming in, um, so you're gonna see in me someone that values,"],[1402,"uh, those relations with the people in the legislature. I'm 3rd in leadership. In my own caucus and also have done a number I'm not gonna go through all the campaign talking points, but I was #1 for bipartisan bills, #3 for passing bills into law. You don't get to that stage in the US Senate if you don't understand the value of working with people both on the Republican side and in the same caucus that you maybe don't always agree with, and I'm gonna put a huge priority on this."],[1433,"As we set our priorities going forward, because I believe for our state the stakes couldn't be more high right now. -- I promise right here -- you said you want to sign the bill in the House. Uh, legislative leader said last told us last night that you indicated to them that you wanted those proposals to come early to get to the first year desk. Is that true? Or if not, what else? Like, do you want to see those some of the first policies. Well, I think the gun safety bill is going to get passed,"],[1464,"and I am so excited to be working with the leaders on this, and it certainly should be one of our top priorities. Um, of course, we're going to have a number of proposals here when it comes to growth and bringing costs down. So I just want to make it clear there's going to be a number of priorities at the beginning. Um, last night, um, at my event that we had before the bigger one. Um, with the, um, that you were all at, um, uh, where are the Moisky, Harper's parents, they were there this morning."],[1495,"One of the first texts that I got, uh, was from, uh, little Fletcher Merkel's parents. Last night, yesterday was Harper's birthday, and those parents, they wanted to be there because they understood that through their grief, uh, that they were going to take that grief and they were going to turn it into action to save the lives of other children in the future. I think that bill, uh, makes a lot of sense. I'm sure that we'll make some changes and work with him on it. Um, but the basics of that bill, I hope will remain in place."],[1528,"I got it. He moderated the very hot housing forum, the hottest event we did, and so I must turn to him in a cooler atmosphere. you're already hear in this one too. Um, when you look at getting your first budget done, uh, next year with those leaders, you're committed to not having new new tax increases, of course, the leaders had different vision under the last trifecta. How do you square that? Do you see any pressure points? Uh, when it comes to raising revenue for the state taxes, you know, I want to see where we are revenue like, but I have been very, very firm on this."],[1559,"I'm not going to raise taxes, and that is not going to change. Um, I think that, um, Minnesota's year has been going better than some people thought for growth. Um, we are, you know, we've been lagging for growth. We all know this. We've been at 1.6%, um, per year compared to 2.4% for the rest of the country. Um, but this year, and we'll see if it remains, I, I don't have those numbers, but in the first two quarters, uh, we were at 3% growth, which was 6th in the nation."],[1590,"Um, but that I think we all know that we have had a long term problem of not expanding enough, not bringing in enough businesses, which is why this was and will be my priority. This may help some with the budget, with some of the forecasts we saw in the past, um, but it does. Doesn't change at all my focus on getting through the red tape, making changes to the state government, um, and not raising taxes given where we are, uh, nationally on that front and trying to reduce some taxes,"],[1621,"especially the ones that are really hitting. Um, the people who are hurting right now because of, uh, what Donald Trump has done. OK, yep, hm, wait, are you the minority negotiations? I, of course, I'm going to work with the minority on legislative negotiations. Governor Klobuchar, um, how do you propose having Minnesotans, um, know that hold you accountable for the top"],[1651,"to bottom audit with other areas like housing? You have a very clear number 100,000 units, 10,000 jobs. Is there like a dollar figure we should expect to be saved from the top to bottom audit? How do we kind of hold you accountable for that? So, uh, that's a. Really good question. I've thought a lot about this, um, because I think a lot of this will be transparency in terms of what's going on. I think one of the hardest things for the public right now, I'm well aware of how these criminal cases work, right? Fraud that maybe occurred 3 years ago or 2 years ago,"],[1682,"and we actually changed the, uh, the legislature, I should. Say I'm not there yet, uh, but I supported this, uh, with Attorney General Ellison's suggestion was to change the statute of limitations on Medicaid fraud prosecutions. I actually think we should expand it to other kinds of prosecutions given what we now know is going on. So why do I say all that? Well, these cases are going to keep coming out, right? And that means that law enforcement, local, federal, state are just doing their jobs, and that's really good."],[1713,"So, I want the public to know that there are going to continue to be prosecutions. And one of the things that I think I could do to make it be very clear that this doesn't mean that we're suddenly having more and more fraud. It simply means we're doing our job in cleaning it up is to routinely. Report to the public on what the status of this is how many prosecutions we see going on in the federal level, the status of the case, this is what's going on on the state level. This is what we've done in the agencies."],[1743,"We have changed these team members. We are going to update the technology. We got 90 million down from last year, and this is what we want to do next. So I think really giving them some fulsome information to all of you. So that they have that information is going to be really important because it's just not going to be fixed in one minute when you have ongoing cases and we have to put the team. But what you do have to do is stop the bleed of these fraudsters preying on taxpayers and putting these new procedures in place."],[1775,"I've always been. One to believe based on my previous work as running Minnesota's biggest prosecutor's office, uh, that if people know these fraudsters out there and potential fraudsters know that you are serious about it, that alone reduces fraud when they start seeing what these sentences are. So I think those kinds of reports and getting that information out there, doing some really practical things like the surprise unannounced. Visits, the vetting, some of which is going on now,"],[1805,"and then having better checks through technology on the system and putting in new leaders is going to be important because as you know, this is also going on in other parts of the country. Um, as these fraud rings prey on different state programs, Governor, -- what are your thoughts -- on an Equal Rights Amendment? That was one of the legislature was trying to get through a couple of years ago, and it's specifically language on pregnancy outcomes. OK, well, yes, I'm very, I'm looking forward to working with them on that. I, I believe I've supported the ERA in the past."],[1835,"OK, but anything more? Yes, um, when do you Are you planning to resign your seat from the US Senate, and if it's not until January, are you thinking about who you're going to appoint to fill that seat? Well, first of all, I just won the election last night. Um, and, um, I will be very careful in that decision. Uh, you are right, it is, um, the decision has to be made pretty much before I get in the governor's office or around that time. And so,"],[1865,"uh, stay tuned for that. It is an interim position, uh, because there will be an election for that position, um, and so I will do right by the state of Minnesota with that person. OK, thanks everyone. Thank you."]]},"el-sayed":{"videoId":"Ah-DuMrYvz0","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"right now that means taking on the corporations and the billionaires, special interests who've rigged the system against us for too long.","t":993}],"full":[[null,"Thank you. Friends, you know how we do, money out of?"],[21,"Michigan, we did it. My name is Abdulrahman Mohamed El-Sayed and I am so proud and honored to stand here as your senator elect from the great state of Michigan. Up until right about now, you might have noticed, I always say Inshallah or God willing, whenever the outcome of this race was mentioned. But today, tonight, we can turn that Inshallah into a..."],[null,"Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul."],[90,"For the right wing ops, that just means praise be to God. This movement for money out of politics, money in your pocket and Medicare for all, I just want to thank you everybody who knocked the door, made a call, sent a dollar, posted a story, and most importantly, gave us your stake in democracy. You took a chance on the unlikeliest of candidates. So thank you. This is all yours."],[129,"Michigan, I cannot wait to serve you with the same bigheartedness, open-mindedness, grit and earnestness that you've shown me. You welcome me to your homes, your churches, your synagogues, your VFW and union halls. You shared moments of frustration and sadness and vulnerability with me. You gave me grace and strength in my lowest moments and the hope and inspiration that powered my best. I love you back. And I hope that I can bring it all with me. I hope I can bring it all with me to Washington in your service."],[171,"Thank you for your trust and your belief and your kindness. I'm going to take it all with me and I hope to bring back the kind of leadership that more than earns it. The last month has brought the stakes of this election into sharp relief. Ours, this beautiful movement was built over the past year and a half campaigning across Michigan's biggest cities and its smallest towns. We spoke of a brighter, a bigger, more hopeful Michigan."],[200,"Theirs, an AstroTurfed corporate funded advertising campaign built to deceive and distract."],[215,"Rather than try to unite us to contend with the crisis of gas or groceries, the opposition decided to try to divide us. At first, they pointed to my name and my faith as if to say he's a little different. And when it didn't work, they tried to guilt me by association. And when that didn't work, they went all in on one of the ugliest campaigns we've seen in our lifetimes."],[247,"They might have been pointing to my name and my faith, but we all know that my name and my faith aren't the reason you can't afford your gas. Not the reason you can't afford your groceries. Not the reason you can't see a doctor. Now, as I was campaigning, some of you would come up and ask, \"How come you don't hit back? How come you don't call them racist or hateful?\" Because here's the thing, I didn't run for myself. And in truth, they weren't targeting me. They weren't just attacking me. They were targeting and attacking you. They were targeting and attacking the very idea of America."],[292,"See, they hate the idea of an America big enough for anyone who looks a little different or prays a little different or whose family comes from a different part of the world. That includes me, but it also includes anyone and everyone who doesn't look like them, pray like them, love like them, or isn't rich like them. So they turned this race into a simple choice. They want an America that is too small for some of us. We know that America is big enough for all of us, big enough to take on the crises that we face. Day by day, Trump's insults became uglier and coarser. But I got to spend those days with you learning about your struggles, your hopes, and the things that inspire you."],[338,"A mom of two kids with a genetic lung disease in East Jordan, fighting the system to make sure her kids don't lose the meds that they rely on to stay alive. Her hope that they don't have to struggle with health insurance like she has. A grandma on the East Side fighting to make sure that the violence that took her son doesn't take her grandson too. Her hope, an America where boys get to grow up. I met Josh, the UAW auto worker fighting the corporate bosses who hadn't raised their wages in two decades despite billions in profit. And they won that fight. His hope an America where every single worker gets the right to a union. I met a small business owner fighting to make sure that another heart attack doesn't take food off the table for his 30 employees or their families. His hope that his workers don't have to worry about how they'll feed their families."],[397,"See, I didn't get into this to defend myself. No, I got into it because their fights are my fight and their hopes are all of our hopes. We don't do this work for ourselves. We do this work for each other to defend us all from another generation's youth treasure and opportunity squandered at the altar of endless war. To defend us all from corporate oligarchs who've bought and sold our government to rig the system against us. To defend us all from a healthcare system more interested in monetizing our illness than healing our bodies and minds. To defend us all from air too putrid, to breathe and water, too putrid to drink. To defend us all from losing our voting or our reproductive or our human rights."],[null,"See, I ran to defend us all from politicians who want to divide us rather than movements that work to dignify us. Across our primary and general election campaigns, they spent over, get this, $350 million trying to beat us."],[460,"That is a record here in Michigan. $70 million alone in the primary funded by all the same cats who funded the general election, and that's a record anywhere in this country."],[473,"But y'all, Michigan, we built something bigger than a bank account. We built a movement. A government of the people, by the people and for the people. We showed that in a battle between the money and the many, that the many really can win. And so to all the kids who watched this last month, to all the parents who struggled to explain why the president openly mocked someone for their name or how they pray, let them know tomorrow that the bad guys lost. Let them know."],[null,"Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul. Abdul."],[519,"I want you to let them know, let them know that we together fighting for something bigger, we won. So Mike, enjoy your retirement. I know you got a house in Florida and two yachts. See, you chose hate and Michigan chose hope. May we never have to see the likes of you in this state again. JD, Habibi! There is this delicious irony in the fact that you're constitutionally obligated to swear me in January. So you know what that means? Wolverine one, Buckeye zero. Donald, look, I know you struggled with my name. So after JD swears me in January, you could just go on and call me Senator."],[602,"To the Super PACs and special interests who tried to beat us, we are coming for your system of politics. To APAC who spent $42 million against us, thank you for giving me the opportunity to beat you twice. And I want to say something here. See, they try to call you hateful if you believe that Palestinian kids should get to grow up in the land of their forefathers, you will not be murdered by our tax dollars. If you believe in equal rights to peace, dignity and self-determination, that's not hate, it's love."],[null,"Michiganders, we want our taxes spent here for schools here and healthcare here and infrastructure here. We don't want our money sent to do apartheid or genocide or war. Michiganders believe in Michigan and I believe in Michiganders and I am so honored that Michiganders believed in me. See, you took a bet on the least likely of candidates. I'm not a politician. I'm a doctor with an 11 letter first name. They told us when I started this campaign, there was no way to beat the money. They told us that someone with a name and my story, a Muslim, was unelectable, let alone in a statewide Senate race in Michigan."],[690,"They told us that old fashioned politics was dead, that traveling the state to have real conversations with real people in real places was a fool's errand. They told us that the establishment was too strong, that DC was going to dictate who won and who lost, that Washington and its special interests didn't want us. They told us that when all the votes had been counted on August 4th and then again on November 3rd, it would have been time and money and energy wasted."],[714,"Guess what? It's November 3rd and the votes have been counted. And guess what we just showed them? That a movement of the people by the people and for the people will ultimately win. Michigan understands the solidarity. It's the people who decide who we send to Washington and what Washington will do. We decide not the big money or their stooges. The people of Michigan will be heard."],[742,"We showed that we together, we can defeat a record $70 million of outside spending, an 11:1 money disadvantage in a primary election, that we can defeat a quarter of a billion dollars in a general election. We can defeat the cynicism of a politics that preys on our earnestness, undersells our intelligence and exploits our disagreements. Tonight, Michigan, we beat a machine and we prove once again just how big America really is because where else, where else but in America can a doctor named Abdulrahman Mohamed El-Sayed, a child of immigrants raised by his father and his daughter of the American Revolution stepmother get elected senator from America's greatest state?"],[795,"They tried to confuse you. So let me just set the record straight. I love America. I know exactly what America gave to me. I saw it up close on trips to my family's native Egypt. In a 15-hour journey, I'd crossed 10 years difference in life expectancy. I didn't have to go 15 hours. I could go 15 minutes to Detroit or Pontiac and cross that same difference. This is why I became a doctor. America vaccinated me against diseases that killed an aunt and uncle I never got to meet. It gave me incredible public schools. It gave me a public university education. It paid my medical education through the NIH. I love America. But I love America enough to ask her to be America for all her kids."],[850,"See, America is not just a flag, not just our red, white and blue. It's not a few patriotic songs that we sing or even a landmass we call home. America is about these truths that we hold, that all people are created equal and the inalienable rights we still struggle to guarantee. Life, liberty, the pursuit of happiness. The best of America lives in the audacity of daring a contradiction, a more perfect union that despite the fact that you can't be more than perfect, we embrace the work of perfecting. America's greatness lives in the moments of free people come together to expand that field of freedom."],[898,"America's greatness is the fight to erase the longstanding consequences of slavery and Jim Crow and segregation. America's greatness is the fight to embrace all of her people regardless how they pray or if they pray, who they love or how they identify. America's greatness is in the union struggle on a shop floor to push off the yoke of greed. America's greatness is the fight to guarantee all of us the healthcare we need if we get sick. Our greatness is the fight for clean air, clean water and a good home. Our greatness is the fight for equal pay, for equal work and full freedom of our bodies. America's greatness is in the belief a new American still has in the hope that America has always represented."],[947,"America's greatness isn't about ignoring our flaws. It's the courage that we have to correct them. Michigan, it just shouldn't be this hard. Shouldn't be this hard to buy a second bag of groceries or fill your tank. Shouldn't be this hard to afford a home. It shouldn't be this hard to see a doctor in the richest, most powerful country in the world. It shouldn't be this hard to pay your taxes and know that that money's going to be spent on you and your kids instead of dropping bombs on somebody else and their kids."],[957,"Shouldn't be this hard. We don't need to be great again. We need to embrace that thing about us that has always made us great, the will to be more perfect. And right now that means taking on the corporations and the billionaires, special interests who've rigged the system against us for far too long. Now before I close, I've got some thank yous I've got to get through."],[null,"Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah. Sarah."],[null,"Sarah, thank you. Thank you for everything. There is no doing this without you and I wouldn't want to do it with anyone else. I love you and I'm so grateful for you. Emmalee and Serene, been my inspiration the entire time. I hope someday that they get to read about this in the history books to understand just how big a part of it they really were. To my parents and my parents in love, my grandparents, my siblings, my extended family, I can never really repay all that you've poured into me. Thank you always for having my back, even if you'd rather I was a surgeon."],[1071,"To my incredible campaign team, y'all, we did it. I asked you to lift me up and hold me down and you did both with grace, humility, kindness, and efficiency. No one else I'd rather ride with, best team in American politics. To all the incredible endorsers who entrusted me with your name, who took time out of your schedule to come campaign with us, to the Michigan Dems who threw this amazing event for us tonight, our chair, Curtis Hertel, who's had our back thick and thin. To all the council people and mayors, all the commissioners and county leaders, state reps and state senators, congresspeople and US senators, thank you for standing with us."],[1117,"And a special thank you to our sisters and brothers in labor. Your support as a second generation union member has meant more than you can imagine. I cannot wait to stand with you in the fight for Michigan's working people. For all the community outreach organizations that came through for us in the final stretch, I cannot imagine doing this without you. Thank you so much."],[1143,"And to all of us here, this fight is not yet over. The day I jumped into this race, I promised you that I'd put in the work, fight the fights on your behalf. I asked you for your time, your energy, your support over the last 19 months. Now I'm asking you to support us for the next six years."],[1165,"This work is bigger than one senator. It's about changing the face of our politics. So please do not send me to DC all by myself. All right, I need y'all to come with me. Winning a single US Senate seat was never the goal. The goal is to use that seat to transform our politics because it's high passed time that we get money out of?"],[1197,"The beauty and soul of America is that we the people are what America is all about. We deserve an America for all of her kids. So Michigan, let's go build it. Thank you so much."]]},"flanagan":{"videoId":"dgbqL21JhAw","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"No more selling this country off to the highest bidder.","t":72},{"text":"we will rip ICE apart","t":744},{"text":"we have the opportunity to replace it","t":772}],"full":[[31,"ALL RIGHT. MINNESOTA YOU JUST BEAT DONALD TRUMP. AMERICA DID TOO. YOU SAID NO MORE WAR, NO MORE HEALTHCARE CUTS, NO MORE TAKING FOOD AWAY FROM CHILDREN AND SENIORS. NO MORE SELLING THIS COUNTRY OFF TO THE HIGHEST BIDDER. AND YOU SAID NO MORE MASKED GOONS SHOOTING OUR NEIGHBORS. YOU SAID NO MORE BALLROOMS, NO MORE BOMBS OR TAX BREAKS FOR BILLIONAIRES. THE GRIP NOW AND THE TAKING BACK OUR COUNTRY FROM THE GRIP OF THE MOST CORRUPT ADMINISTRATION IN OUR NATION'S HISTORY STARTS TONIGHT."],[129,"BECAUSE ALL ACROSS THIS STATE AND ALL ACROSS THIS COUNTRY, PEOPLE ARE SAYING ENOUGH IS. THEY'RE SAYING THAT WORKING PEOPLE DESERVE AN ECONOMY AND A COUNTRY THAT FINALLY WORKS FOR THEM, NOT DONALD TRUMP AND HIS BILLIONAIRE BESTIES. IT IS TIME TO END THE TRUMP ERA OF CHAOS, CRUELTY, AND CORRUPTION. AND FRIENDS, IT IS TIME FOR NEW VOICES TO SHAKE UP OUR PARTY AND TAKE BACK. HELP PEOPLE IT IS TIME TO HELP PEOPLE AFFORD THE LIVES THEY WANT TO LIVE."],[185,"LET TODAY BE THE START OF A NEW AMERICAN MOVEMENT. IT IS A MOVEMENT THAT IS DEFINED NOT BY CORPORATE GREED OR POLITICAL HATRED, BUT BY THE POWER OF PEOPLE COMING TOGETHER TO DEMAND CHANGE. AND WE SAW IT COMING, MINNESOTA. BECAUSE IT BEGAN RIGHT HERE. WHEN A PRESIDENT WHO THINKS HE'S A KING SENT THUGS TO OUR STATE, YOU SENT HIS PRIVATE ARMY PACKING. IN THE IN THE DEAD OF WINTER. YOU VENTURE TO LEAVE THE SAFETY OF YOUR HOME."],[239,"YOU PICKED UP GROCERIES FOR PEOPLE YOU DIDN'T KNOW. YOU WALKED KIDS TO SCHOOL WHO WEREN'T YOURS. YOU MARCHED, YOU BLEW WHISTLES. YOU BELIEVE THAT YOUR NEIGHBORS ARE ALWAYS WORTH FIGHTING FOR. AND YOU PROVED. YOU PROVED THAT WHEN MINNESOTANS FIGHT FOR ONE ANOTHER, WE CAN INSPIRE A NATION TO JOIN THAT FIGHT BECAUSE WHEN YOU COME FOR ONE OF US, YOU COME FOR ALL. AND WE ARE NOT, WE ARE NOT JUST THE LAND OF 10,000 LAKES."],[302,"WE ARE THE LAND OF 5.8 MILLION NEIGHBORS. AND TO BE A MINNESOTAN IS TO BELIEVE IN FAIRNESS ABOVE ALL ELSE. IT MOVES US TO ACT FOR ONE ANOTHER, AND TODAY WE CHOSE CHANGE. ALL ACROSS THE COUNTRY TODAY, PEOPLE SPOKE LOUDLY AND CLEARLY, AND THE POWERFUL SURE BETTER LISTEN. WHETHER THE PEOPLE PUT UP SIGNS FOR A PEDIATRICIAN IN SOUTH CAROLINA. OR MADE CALLS FOR A FORMER SCHOOL TEACHER IN TEXAS."],[352,"WHETHER THEY KNOCKED ON DOORS FOR A PARALYMPIAN LEGISLATOR IN IOWA. OR FOR A LOGGER IN MAINE. A METHODIST MINISTER IN KANSAS. OR A MUSLIM AMERICAN DOCTOR IN MICHIGAN. OR WHETHER THEY VOTED FOR THE DAUGHTER OF A NAVY VETERAN AND SCHOOL TEACHER IN CHICAGO. OR WORK THEIR HEARTS OUT FOR THIS IRISH CATHOLIC NATIVE AMERICAN FROM. WE KNOW THAT PEOPLE DEMANDED MORE, AND FOR THOSE OF US ELECTED IN THIS MOMENT, IT IS OUR DUTY TO DELIVER."],[423,"AND YOU BETTER BELIEVE THAT CHANGE IS GOING TO COME. IT'S GOING TO COME FROM NEW VOICES THAT WEREN'T PICKED BY THE ESTABLISHMENT OR PARTY LEADERS. WE WE WERE PICKED BY THE PEOPLE. WE FOUGHT BACK AGAINST THE MONEY. WE TOOK ON OUR OWN PARTY AND WE ARE THE ONES WHO ARE GOING TO SHAKE UP THE STATUS QUO. WE WERE OVERLOOKED AND UNDERESTIMATED, BUT WE WILL NOT BE STOPPED. BOOHO PEGGY FLANAGAN AND JISHINAAZ GIJIWERU DAUWE AND TO GO KABABIDIGANIKAD AND DUJABA."],[498,"MY INGAN IN DODE. SO THE NAME YOU VOTED FOR ON THE BALLOT SAYS PEGGY FLANAGAN, BUT MY OJIBWE NAME SPEAKS IN A LOUD AND CLEAR VOICE, WOMAN. I AM A PROUD DAUGHTER OF THE WHITE EARTH NATION. AND MY FAMILY IS THE WOLF CLAN. AND THE ROLE OF OUR PLAN IS TO ENSURE WE NEVER LEAVE ANYONE BEHIND. AND THAT'S BEEN THE PURPOSE OF OUR CAMPAIGN. WE REFUS LET THIS COUNTRY LEAVE ANYONE BEHIND. AND HERE'S THE DEAL, OUR CAMPAIGN DIDN'T BEGIN IN A WASHINGTON DC CONFERENCE ROOM."],[554,"BUT AT A KITCHEN TABLE IN SAINT LOUIS PARK. AND IT GREW IT GREW IN THE BASEMENT OF THE HIBBING PUBLIC LIBRARY NEXT TO THE BOB DYLAN EXHIBIT. IN CAFES, IN CHURCHES, IN VFWS, BARNS, GARAGES, UNION HALLS, AND LIVING ROOMS. AND AT THE DARKEST HOUR IN THE WEEKS AND MONTHS AFTER DONALD TRUMP WAS ELECTED. WHEN HE STILL LOOKED UNBEATABLE. YOU TOOK THE BOLDEST ACTION IMAGINABLE. YOU SHOWED UP. AND WE TOOK OUT OUR FLIP CHART PAPER AND WE ASKED EACH OTHER, WHAT WORRIES YOU?"],[609,"WHO ARE YOU FIGHTING FOR AND WHAT BRINGS YOU HOPE? AND WE EVEN PUT IT ON POST-IT NOTES, AND WE SHARED OUR STORIES. AND PEOPLE ALL ACROSS THE STATE HAVE CONTINUED TO SHARE THEIR STORIES WITH ME EVERY DAY SINCE. LIKE JESSICA, A LIBRARIAN MARRIED TO A FARMER IN CAMBY WHO HAS A $16,000 DEDUCTIBLE AND HAD TO PAY $600 FOR A 5 MINUTE MED CHECK. OR MAGGIE IN MOORHEAD, WHO WORKS THE NIGHT SHIFT AT A HOTEL AND THEN GETS UP IN THE MORNING TO RUN A BAKERY THE NEXT DAY BECAUSE ONE JOB ISN'T ENOUGH."],[655,"IT SHOULD BE OR MY BUDDY BENTLEY, WHO I MET IN BRAINER. WHO RELIES ON MEDICAID TO SURVIVE. HIS MOM CHRIS LIVES IN FEAR OF WHAT DONALD TRUMP'S CUTS TO MEDICAID WILL MEAN FOR HER CHILD, AND SHE IS ONE OF THE BEST MOMS I HAVE EVER MET IN MY ENTIRE LIFE. IT IS THE PEOPLE OF MINNESOTA. THAT SAW A SPACE TO FIGHT BACK IN THIS CAMPAIGN. YOU POWERED US TO VICTORY AND YOU MADE OUR MISSION CLEAR."],[693,"YOU FOUGHT FOR ME AND NOW I'M GOING TO FIGHT FOR YOU. SO FRIENDS IN WASHINGTON, HERE'S WHAT I'M GONNA THROW DOWN FOR. WE ARE GOING TO LOWER COSTS SO THAT FAMILIES CAN AFFORD THEIR LIVES. WE'RE GOING TO GET RID OF PRIOR AUTHORIZATION SO THAT SOME DUDE BEHIND A DESK. WORSE YET, AN AI BOT CAN'T DETERMINE WHETHER OR NOT YOU GET THE LIFE SAVING HEALTHCARE THAT YOUR DOCTOR HAS PRESCRIBED."],[733,"WE WILL PASS RIGHT TO REPAIR SO THAT FARMERS CAN FIX THEIR OWN DAMN EQUIPMENT. WE WILL RIP ICE APART. AND WE, WE HAVE THE OPPORTUNITY TO REPLACE IT WITH AN IMMIGRATION SYSTEM THAT IS GROUNDED IN PUBLIC SAFETY FOR EVERYBODY. DIGNITY AND DUE PROCESS, WHICH BY THE WAY, IS STILL A PART OF OUR CONSTITUTION. A SYSTEM THAT DOES NOT TEAR CHILDREN AWAY FROM THEIR FAMILIES. WE WILL STOP WASHINGTON'S CORRUPTION AND HOLD THE MOST CORRUPT ADMINISTRATION IN OUR NATION'S HISTORY ACCOUNTABLE EVERY DAY."],[813,"AND WE WILL END DONALD TRUMP'S RECKLESS WAR IN IRAN. AND HEAR ME NOW, WE WILL PASS MEDICARE FOR ALL. AND LISTEN PEOPLE WILL TELL US THAT WE ARE DREAMING TOO BIG AND THAT WE ARE ASKING FOR TOO MUCH. DO NOT LISTEN TO THEM. ALL OF THIS IS POSSIBLE, FRIENDS, BECAUSE WE KNOW THAT WE GET WHAT WE ORGANIZE FOR. IN AND I HAVE TO SAY THAT I CAN'T QUITE BELIEVE. THAT I AM STANDING HERE. AS YOUR NEXT UNITED STATES SENATOR FROM M MY HEART MY HEART IS SO FULL. MY HEART IS SO FULL."],[919,"AND I'M ALSO THINKING A LOT ABOUT MY MOM. WE LOST HER SHORTLY AFTER THE 2022 ELECTION. AND WHILE SHE HASN'T BEEN ON THIS EARTHLY PLANE, SHE HAS BEEN RIGHT HERE WITH ME ALONG THIS ENTIRE JOURNEY. IT'S PAT FLANAGAN'S STRENGTH AND RESILIENCE THAT GAVE ME THE COURAGE AND THE CONVICTION TO BELIEVE THAT A KID LIKE ME COULD ONE DAY STAND ON A STAGE LIKE THIS ONE. AND IT WAS MY DAD, MARVIN MANYPENNY, WHO TAUGHT ME TO SPEAK TRUTH TO POWER."],[969,"HE USED TO SAY, MY GIRL. I WANT TO BURN THE SYSTEM DOWN. I WANT TO CHANGE IT FROM THE INSIDE OUT. WELL, MINNESOTA, THAT'S WHAT WE DID TONIGHT. THAT IS WHAT WE ARE GOING TO KEEP DOING TOGETHER. WE'RE GOING TO CHANGE THE HELL OUT OF THE SYSTEM AND FINALLY MAKE IT WORK. BECAUSE YOU PROVED THAT ONCE AGAIN THE MANY CAN BEAT THE MONEY AND NO PRESIDENT CAN EVER BEAT THE POWER OF THE PEOPLE."],[1015,"YOU SAID LOUD AND CLEAR THAT WE REFUSE TO SETTLE FOR LEFTOVERS. AND YOU YOU HELPED A SMALL BUT SCRAPPY, OFTEN UNDERESTIMATED, ENROLLED MEMBER OF THE WHITE EARTH NATION. BECAUSE WOMAN IN HISTORY TO BE ELECTED TO THE TO THE YOUNG PEOPLE OUT THERE. WHO LOOK LIKE ME TO THE DAUGHTERS AND TO THE SONS WHO TOO OFTEN ARE FORGOTTEN OR ERASED. I SEE DO NOT BE DISHEARTENED THAT IT TOOK 250 YEARS FOR ONE OF US TO GET HERE."],[1097,"BE INSPIRED BY THE FACT THAT WITH GRIT AND DETERMINATION AND THE RESILIENCE OF OUR PEOPLE, WHICHEVER ONE OF YOU IS NEXT, YOU'RE GONNA GET HERE A LOT FASTER. BECAUSE IF AUNTIE PEGGY CAN DO IT, YOU CAN DO IT TOO. AND PEOPLE PEOPLE WILL UNDERESTIMATE YOU, MY GIRL. DO NOT LET THEM. YOU KNOW WHO YOU ARE, YOU KNOW WHERE YOU COME FROM, AND YOU KNOW WHAT YOU CAN DO. THERE IS NO STOPPING YOU FROM ACHIEVING YOUR DREAMS."],[1145,"AND THERE IS NO STOPPING MINNESOTA BECAUSE OUR CAUSE IS RIGHTEOUS AND OUR PEOPLE WILL NOT BEND. AND YOU BETTER BELIEVE THAT WE ARE GOING TO FIGHT LIKE HELL FOR OUR STATE AND FOR OUR COUNTRY. AND IT WOULD TAKE ME, IT WOULD TAKE ME WEEKS TO THANK ALL OF THE PEOPLE THAT I NEED TO THANK. BUT I DO WANT TO TAKE A FEW MOMENTS. I WANT TO TAKE A MOMENT TO THANK MICHELLE TAFOYA FOR RUNNING A SPIRITED CAMPAIGN."],[1184,"SHE, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO. SHE CALLED EARLIER TONIGHT AND SHE SAID, I HOPE YOU DO RIGHT BY MINNESOTA, AND I SAID, YOU BET. I WANT TO THANK MY CAMPAIGN TEAM. LED BY A BADASS MINNESOTA. FROM NEWALM WHO RAN A SMALL BUT MIGHTY TEAM THAT HELD 360 EVENTS IN 125 COMMUNITIES. AND SHE SHE DID IT IN THE FACE OF UNIMAGINABLE TRAGEDIES AND UNPRECEDENTED MONEY SPENT AGAINST US. THANK YOU, PEYTON LEWIS. AND THANK YOU TO THE CAMPAIGN TEAM THAT YOU LED TO VICTORY."],[1244,"YOU SLAYED. AND TO MEGAN SHANNON. OUR DEPUTY CAMPAIGN MANAGER, WHOSE PROBLEM SOLVING ABILITIES KNOW NO BOUNDS AND CAN ALWAYS SOLVE PROBLEMS AND KNOWS WHICH DIRECTION FLAGS SHOULD FACE. I THANK YOU SO MUCH AND TO NOODLE, WE CAN'T WAIT TO MEET YOU. AND TO EVERY SINGLE VOLUNTEER WHOSE HARD WORK POWERED THIS ENTIRE CAMPAIGN. THANK YOU, THANK YOU, THANK YOU. AND THANK YOU, SENATOR TINA SMITH."],[1306,"THANK YOU FOR BEING A MENTOR AND A FRIEND. AND AN INSPIRATION. THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING YOU'VE DONE FOR ME AND FOR THE PEOPLE OF MINNESOTA. YOU ARE LEAVING SOME AWFULLY BIG CHUCK TAYLOR'S TO FILL, SISTER. I LOVE YOU SO MUCH. AND THANK YOU TO GOVERNOR TIM WALSH. I AM GRATEFUL FOR ALL OF THE WORK THAT WE DID TOGETHER ON BEHALF OF MINNESOTA'S CHILDREN AND FAMILIES AND THE HISTORIC WORK TO STRENGTHEN TRIBAL-STATE RELATIONS."],[1347,"THANK YOU, GOVERNOR, FOR YOUR SERVICE TO MINNESOTA. AND LAST BUT NEVER EVER LEAST. TOM AND SIOBHAN. YOU ARE MY INSPIRATION. TOM, YOU ARE MY PERSON. AND I CANNOT BELIEVE I GOT TO MARRY MY LOCAL CELEBRITY CRUSH. AND THEN EVERY DAY YOU DEFINE WHAT IT MEANS TO BE IN A TRUE PARTNERSHIP. I LOVE YOU. AND TO MY WHOLE HEART, SIOBHAN. MY GIRL I AM SO PROUD OF YOU EVERY SINGLE DAY YOU KNOW WHO YOU ARE."],[1407,"YOUR TALENT, YOUR HEART, YOUR COURAGE, YOUR COMPASSION. YOUR HUMOR KNOWS NO BOUNDS. AND MY PROUDEST ACCOMPLISHMENT EVER WAS BRINGING YOU INTO THE WORLD AND BEING YOUR MOM. I LOVE YOU SO MUCH, MY GIRL. AND TONIGHT, IT'S HARD NOT TO THINK ABOUT MY POLITICAL HERO, PAUL WALLSTONE. PAUL'S LAST CAMPAIGN WAS MY FIRST, AND HE USED TO ALWAYS SAY, I DON'T REPRESENT THE BIG OIL COMPANIES."],[1449,"I DON'T REPRESENT THE BIG PHARMACEUTICAL COMPANIES. I DON'T REPRESENT THE ENRONS OF THE WORLD. BUT YOU KNOW WHAT? THEY ALREADY HAVE GREAT REPRESENTATION IN WASHINGTON. IT'S THE REST OF THE PEOPLE THAT NEED IT. I REPRESENT THE PEOPLE OF MINNESOTA. AND SO I WILL SAY IT THE WAY THAT PAUL DID. YOU WILL ALWAYS KNOW WHERE I STAND AND WHO I STAND UP FOR. WON'T REPRESENT THE BILLIONAIRES."],[1483,"I WON'T REPRESENT THE BIG DRUG COMPANIES OR THE BIG INSURANCE COMPANIES, AND I SURE AS HELL WON'T REPRESENT DONALD TRUMP. I WILL REPRESENT THE PEOPLE OF MINNESOTA WHETHER YOU VOTED FOR ME OR NOT. BECAUSE I HAVE NEVER BEEN MORE PROUD TO BE A MINNESOTAN THAN I AM RIGHT THIS MINUTE. AND FRIENDS, WHEN I GET TO WASHINGTON. I KNOW I'M NOT GOING ALONE. I AM BRINGING ALL OF YOU WITH ME."],[1535,"THANK YOU ALL SO MUCH, GICHI MIGWICH. I LOVE YOU, MINNESOTA."]]},"pappas":{"videoId":"Zq4VEhMyiLA","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"a wake-up call for corporate special interests and billionaires who have been rigging the economy","t":121},{"text":"it's nice to know that love and truth prevailed tonight","t":451}],"full":[[0,"Heat. Heat. [cheering] [cheering] Well, good evening, New Hampshire. This has been a long campaign against a backdrop of the chaos, corruption, and cost coming out of Washington. And New Hampshire showed up today. You you spoke out today. You said in a resounding voice that America needs a course correction. That Washington needs a new generation at the table to fix things. [cheering] And that New Hampshire needs independent leadership to stand up and get stuff done. [cheering] You know, throughout throughout this campaign, you invited me into your homes, your community centers, and your small businesses. You shared with me your challenges, your fears, and your hopes for the future. And tonight, I am honored beyond words to have earned your votes to fight for you in the United States Senate. [cheering]"],[79,"[applause] A few minutes ago, I just got a very gracious call from John Cenounu. He wished us he wished us and our team well, and I wish the same for him and his family. And I think we all owe John Cenounu a big uh debt of gratitude for his public service for the people of New Hampshire. [applause] So tonight, whether you're a Republican, an independent, or a Democrat, tonight's victory is for you because this is a victory for team New Hampshire over the broken status quo that is hurting all of us just the same."],[116,"[cheering and applause] Tonight's results Tonight's results are a wake-up call for corporate special interests and billionaires who have been rigging the economy. For the cowards in Congress who have enabled healthc care cuts, tariffs, and war, and for the incompetent president who can't even be bothered to care how people are being hurt. So tonight, voters in New Hampshire and all across the country simply have had enough and are demanding a change in direction. and I am ready to fight with everything I've got to deliver the change that we need."],[149,"[cheering] So, here in New Hampshire, here in New Hampshire, we are cleareyed about the scale of the challenges that we face and the hard work that it will take to move forward. Whether it's building the housing New Hampshire needs, expanding access to health care and child care, saving social security, protecting our planet, restoring reproductive freedom, rooting out corruption, or holding this administration accountable. We don't have a moment to waste, do we?"],[179,"[cheering] But there will of course be moments that test our resolve. There will be times when we hit roadblocks and got get frustrated with the pace of progress. But we can never give up. and we must be commi committed to renewing the purpose of American democracy and working with persistence and urgency each and every day. I'll be honored to stand with the people of New Hampshire shoulderto-shoulder in that work. And I'll work with anyone who can deliver a better life for Granite Sters and to and I'll stand up to anyone who will take us back. You know, across this state, Granite Sters are showing the fighting spirit, the resilience, and the determination that we're known for."],[217,"Protesting against the reckless policies coming out of Washington, organizing against corporate landlords buying up homes and jacking up the rent, opposing big data centers that harm our communities and our well-being, and stopping an ICE detention center from being built in the state of New Hampshire. [cheering] [applause] We're also a state We're also a state that shows compassion, mobilizing for our friends and neighbors, for veterans, for folks struggling with addiction or families who are in need of food or shelter. That's how we do things in the state of New Hampshire. We step up, we roll up our sleeves, and we make it happen. And that's the spirit I'll bring to my work in the United States Senate for all of you. [cheering]"],[264,"So tonight, tonight we don't celebrate a victory for any one political party. We celebrate a victory for anyone left, right, or center struggling with the skyrocketing costs of living from gas to groceries to housing. Anyone who's sick of the tariffs, the endless war, the tax breaks for big corporations paid for by cuts to your healthcare. Anyone who's fed up with the most corrupt president in our history, who has failed in his way of governing. and anyone who knows that we can do so much better if we work together. So, we know this was a hard-fought victory tonight. It was made even harder by the tens and tens of millions of dollars that poured into New Hampshire from Donald Trump, Elon Musk, and corporate special interests who are just fine who are just fine with the way things are going right now. They threw money, attack ads, and outright lies at us every day for months."],[314,"But we beat him anyway, didn't we? [cheering] We were never We were never the big money campaign. We're the people peoplepowered campaign. A campaign of 200,000 individual donors and not a dime from corporate packs. [cheering] And we showed what happens when we stick together, stand up for what's right, and never lose hope, even when the odds are long. It was 579 days ago that we gathered in this very room. A place where we've celebrated many victories with more to come tonight. And a place that has taught me everything about serving the community that I know and love that has given me so many opportunities in my life. Nearly 20 months ago, I said I knew we were living in deeply uncertain times. But I knew something else. That granite sters don't flinch. We don't give in. We stand up and fight. And that's exactly what we did in this campaign. [applause] The fight we started in this room and took to every corner of New Hampshire is now headed to Washington to get our state and our country on the right track for the future. [cheering] And so and so I'll end tonight by saying this."],[387,"I am so grateful for everyone in this room and beyond who made this win possible. I want to thank my extended family who has always shown up for me each and every day. To my amazing parents who have set the best example of public service and hard work and giving back to the community and unconditional love. I want to thank the guy next to me, my amazing husband, Van. [cheering]"],[418,"[cheering] How about it? [cheering] All right. The wrong person was on the ballot apparently, but he's always been by my side. And look, tonight, win, lose, or draw, I'm the luckiest guy because I'm married to a man that I love. [cheering] And despite [applause] all the negative attacks and the lies, it's nice to know that love and truth prevailed tonight. [cheering] I want to thank my amazing campaign staff, led by our campaign manager, Rachel Petri, [cheering]"],[465,"who ran the most effective campaign our state has seen. [cheering] I want to thank Beth Kuniff and all the organizers at organizing for New Hampshire for the work you did to get out the vote. [cheering] You worked hard over the past year uh communicating with voters on the issues that matter and you got it done. I want to thank to our f thank our friends in organized labor as well who stood shouldertoshoulder with us in this campaign [cheering] and I can't wait to continuing to work with all of you to build a fairer future for everyone who calls New Hampshire home. Thank you to all the volunteers, the folks who chipped in, who knocked on doors, who made phone calls, who got voters rides to the polls, who talked to your friends and neighbors about the stakes. I wouldn't be standing before you giving this speech tonight if it weren't for the thousands of folks who have stepped up for this campaign. Thanks for being a part of this. [cheering]"],[518,"And I want to thank the team in my congressional office, too, led by Steven Carlson and Carrie Thurman. [cheering] They've they've spent the past eight years stepping up for Granite Sters and meeting the needs of our constituents and the entire district. And I just salute them for all their hard work on behalf of New Hampshire. [cheering] I want to thank my friend of the New Hampshire delegation, the amazing Senator Maggie Hassen for joining us here tonight. [cheering] It's going to be an honor to be with her as part of the team in the United States Senate working closely together for the people of this state. And I want to send my best wishes to my friend Maggie Goodlander on her victory tonight."],[563,"[cheering and applause] And my friend who I think you'll be hearing from shortly, Stephanie Shaheen. [cheering] [applause] Look, before I close, I just want to recognize someone who is important to all of us here in this room and who's made an immeasurable difference for the people of New Hampshire throughout her time in public service. And that's the great Senator Gene Shaheen. [cheering]"],[590,"[applause] [applause] [cheering] Senator Shaheen has set the standard we should all strive for in public service and I couldn't be more grateful to call her a colleague and a friend. We know that New Hampshire is a better place because of the work she's done throughout her career and her impact on education, on health care, on the environment, the economy, and so many other crucial issues will stand the test of time. So know this, no one will ever fill her shoes, but we all got to carry on her good work, don't we? [cheering]"],[628,"[applause] So tonight we celebrate and as we celebrate, let's think about the brighter future that we can all build together. Let's remember what is possible when we join with common purpose and fight for a fairer, freer New Hampshire. Today, you all did your part. We all did our part to put our state and our country on a better path. And tomorrow, we've got to get to work to fight for what's right and deliver the solutions that are desperately needed. So, my my uh words to you tonight are thank you and let's keep going. Let's keep going. [cheering] Let's keep going and fighting and working for the people of this great state. Thank you all for being here tonight. I really appreciate it."],[670,"[music] [music]"]]},"andrews":{"videoId":"UKe4TxEoTzk","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"in a politics dominated by billionaires and special interest groups and insiders in Washington, DC","t":30},{"text":"She told me it cost $1900 to fill up her tractor with diesel","t":331}],"full":[[0,"I, I, I think we just made some history. So, South Carolina. You You have shown the nation what is possible. You have shown the nation that in this era of partisan divides, of vitriol and name-calling. In a politics dominated by billionaires and special interest groups and insiders in Washington DC that we will not bow down. That we will not back down and we will chart our own course."],[52,"You have shown the nation that we can come together to defend South Carolina. And today you have elected a senator that will always put South Carolina first. Not only that, but you have elected the first pediatrician to the United States Senate. That's right. The first woman that South Carolina has ever sent to the United States Senate. So, from the bottom of my heart, thank you."],[107,"I want to start by thanking Darlene Graham for her public service and her love for South Carolina, and I wish her and her family well. And I, and I just, and I just spoke with her and she congratulated me on our victory tonight. And to the heartbeat, the heartbeat of our campaign, our volunteers. Who worked their tails off and never stopped believing, thank you, thank you, thank you."],[146,"And to our state party chairwoman, Crystal Spain. The first black woman to lead our state's party. Who invested in this race, who believed in us, who believed in me, and worked tirelessly, tirelessly to build a stronger South Carolina across all 46 counties. Thank you, Crystal. And to my dear friend Jamie Harrison, we would not be here without you. Thank you so much. To all of our incredible staff who poured their hearts and souls into this race, thank you."],[195,"To the thousands of people who welcomed us into their homes, their churches, their businesses, and onto their front porches, thank you so much. And to the Republicans, Independents, and Democrats who took a chance on a pediatrician and a mom of three. Because you believe that South Carolina should come first, thank you. South Carolina, my name may have been on the ballot, but this victory doesn't belong to me. It belongs to all of you."],[233,"Because tonight we here in South Carolina sent a clear message that this Senate seat does not belong to one family, one party, or to Washington DC. It belongs to you and it always will. We embarked on this journey over 18 months ago, and while it was long and exhausting, And there were plenty of days when I was running on nothing but protein bars, coffee, and giant Diet Cokes from gas stations. It truly has been the journey of a lifetime."],[270,"We took this campaign to every single one of our 46 counties, from small towns and main streets to farms and our rural communities, from the Blue Ridge Mountains in the upstate to the swamps, the literal swamps in the Midlands, to the beaches here in the Low Country. I sat on the back of a pickup truck with an 8th generation farmer in Barnwell who told me that it now costs her $1900."],[326,"Y'all, I thought my farmer friend was here. She told me it cost $1900 to fill up her tractor with diesel, and that tank of gas will only last her for three days, and that farm that's been in her South Carolina family for eight generations might not last another year or two if things don't change. I've stood shoulder to shoulder with veterans in Ridgeland, tears in their eyes as they told me that they've lost friends to suicide, that their fight for their benefits that they've earned, and their fear of another generation being sent off to a reckless war."],[362,"I've spoken to seniors who've worked their entire lives, raised their family, and did everything right, only to find themselves struggling to get by on their Social Security checks. I've seen neighbors looking out for each other regardless of political party, families coming together to help each other through hard times, and church congregations opening their hearts and doors to anyone who needs a helping hand. This is the South Carolina that I know."],[387,"This is the South Carolina that I am proud to call home. And this is the South Carolina that I will fight for every single day in the United States Senate. And to the South Carolinians who did not vote for me, I know we may not agree on everything, and I may not have earned your vote today, but I want you to know this, I will be your senator too. I will listen to you. I will show up for you, and I will fight just as hard for you and your children as I would my own. That's the kind of senator that I'll be."],[437,"I'll be an independent voice who will work with anyone, Republican or Democrat, to do what's right for South Carolina. I will be a brick wall between Washington DC and South Carolina, even when it means standing up to my own party. Nobody in Washington recruited me to run. Nobody handed me a seat in the United States Senate. And nobody wrote me a script. I, I, I owe no one in Washington anything."],[473,"I owe South Carolina everything. And that's exactly who I'm going to answer to. Now I never imagined that I would end up in politics. Since I was 4, I've only ever dreamed of becoming a doctor, and for the past 20 years, I've dedicated my life to caring for sick and injured children. But what I saw as a pediatrician and what I've experienced raising my own 3 children made me realize that I couldn't just sit on the sidelines anymore."],[504,"I watched as insurance companies stood between sick children and the care that they need. I've seen how decisions made in Washington affect the lives of the children and families I've cared for, and that's why I decided to run, because I believe we have a responsibility to leave our children something better than what we inherited. A South Carolina where a family can afford to fill up a gas tank, put groceries on the table, and get the childcare they need without worrying about going broke."],[536,"When decisions where decisions about our communities are made by the people who live in our communities, not the billionaires or data center companies in Washington DC. And where the next generation can afford to build a life and raise a family here. That's the future that I'm fighting for. And I know that the work ahead won't be easy, but after 18 months in 46 counties and everything we've been through together, I've never been more certain of one thing."],[568,"South Carolina's best days are still ahead of us. And I promise you I'm gonna give you everything I have to make sure we get there, to build a South Carolina you can afford, a South Carolina you can always be proud to call home, and a South Carolina that will always come first. So thank you for believing in me. Thank you for making history with me tonight. And, and most importantly, we had to move this part to the end so I wouldn't be a blubbering idiot up here."],[617,"Most importantly, thank you to my family. To my parents who have stood by me every step of the way. And to my, to my 3 children. Thank you for every hug, every word of encouragement. I love you more. I love you more than words, Henry, than words will ever express. I'm so proud of you guys. And being your mom will always be the most important job I have. Right. All right. And I hope that when you look back on this moment, all three of you, I hope that you remember something that you can stand up for what you believe in."],[681,"That you can speak out when something isn't right. And no matter how big the challenge, you should never be afraid to try to make things better. Because you never know what's possible if you're willing to try. South Carolina, I love you. Thank you and good night."]]},"talarico":{"videoId":"ezPKVpfjMGE","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"We just proved that all the money in the world is no match for the people of Texas.","t":361},{"text":"The real fight in this country is not left versus right. It is top versus bottom.","t":920},{"text":"We will not be conquered.","t":981},{"text":"Texas, it's time to start flipping tables.","t":1440}],"full":[[326,"Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you, Chris. Thank you, Blanca. And thank you all for being here. We just took back Texas. We just proved that all the money in the world is no match for the people of Texas. We just showed that a politics of division is no match for a politics of love."],[385,"And we just sent a message to every billionaire mega donor, every trillionaire mega donor. Every corrupt defender of this broken political system in this state, in this country, power belongs to the people."],[413,"I'm reminded of that story from scripture of a shepherd boy who goes up against a giant. For 40 days, Goliath teases and taunts. On the day of the fight, he shows up in full armor. He's carrying so many weapons. He needs someone else to carry his shield. In this race, we went up against our own Goliaths."],[441,"The richest man in the world, the most powerful man in the world and the entire Washington D.C. establishment. David wasn't as big or as strong as Goliath. He didn't have as many weapons, but he had hope. He had faith and he had a slingshot. You were my slingshot. The people of Texas were my slingshot. And tonight, and tonight we defeated Goliath."],[489,"Scripture has taught me, my own life has taught me, always bet on the underdog. Before I was a politician, I was a public school teacher. I taught language arts at Rhodes Middle School on the west side of San Antonio. And as I always say, teaching middle school is the best preparation for politics."],[513,"The West side is a beautiful historic neighborhood. It's also one of the poorest zip codes in the entire state of Texas. Every day, my students struggled heroically to overcome a rigged system. My students weren't just kids. They were survivors, dreamers, fighters. I saw it in their eyes every day, this unshakeable resolve, this unconquered spirit. Growing up, I saw that same fight in my mother, a preacher's daughter from Laredo who left home at 19."],[557,"She moved up to Austin and met my birth father, a 21-year-old high school dropout whose drinking problem sometimes led to violence. One night he became abusive again, but that night, that night, my mother's love rose to meet that abuse. She packed all our stuff into her little Ford Escort. She drove me to the hotel where she worked. She begged the manager to let us stay in one of the rooms until we found this little apartment in East Austin."],[594,"There wasn't room for a nursery, so I slept in a crib in her closet and she was so proud of that closet. She decorated it with pictures and toys. No one was going to tell her it wasn't a nursery. Always, always bet on the underdog. We were the underdogs in this race. We went up against nearly 40 years of doubt and disillusionment."],[630,"We went up against more than $300 million, more than any Senate campaign in American history. We went up against all the negative ads, smear campaigns, foreign bots and AI deep fakes that money can buy. Those attacks were the final howls of a dying establishment. The death rattle of a status quo that knows its days are numbered."],[668,"They played dirty because they were desperate, but we never lost hope. We never lost faith. And against big money and long odds, we took our power back. Always, always bet on the underdog. We built a movement unlike any this state has ever seen. We united Texans from all backgrounds and beliefs onto one team to take on this broken, corrupt political system. First time voters, three time Trump voters, working people from every corner of this state who are fed up and ready for change."],[717,"This win, this win is for every underdog who's been counted out and left behind. This win is for every teacher and every nurse, for every farmer and every rancher, for every young person who's trying to buy a home, for every parent who's trying to put food on the table. This win, this win is for every Texan who's ever wondered if anyone is listening. I heard you. We heard you. And tonight the world hears you."],[765,"To the Texans who supported this movement, I am humbled by your trust and I will work every day to be worthy of it. And to the Texans who didn't vote for me, I will be your senator too. I will always serve you. I will always fight for you. This win is not about the Democratic Party or the Republican Party. It's much bigger than that."],[796,"There is something broken in America. Our economic system is broken. Our political system is broken. Even our relationships with each other feel broken. That's because the most powerful people in the world want it that way."],[818,"My granddad was a Baptist preacher in South Texas, and when I was little, he told me that we follow a barefoot rabbi who gave us two commandments, love God and love neighbor, because there is no love of God without love of neighbor."],[848,"Every single person bears the image of the sacred. Every single person is holy, not just my neighbor who looks like me, not just my neighbor who prays like me, not just my neighbor who votes like me. I am called to love all of my neighbors the way I love myself."],[875,"Because despite our differences, we all want the same things; a safe neighborhood, a good job, a high quality, well-funded public school, and the ability to see a doctor when we need one. But the billionaires who own the social media algorithms, who own the cable news networks, who own the politicians fighting on our screens, they want us at each other's throats. They want us focused on how we're different instead of on how we're the same. They want us looking left and right at each other instead of looking up at them."],[920,"The real fight in this country is not left versus right. It is top versus bottom. The people at the top work so hard to keep us angry and divided, because our unity is a threat to their wealth and their power. We saw it in this race. We saw it in every billionaire funded attack ad."],[950,"The people at the top divide us by party, by race, by gender, by religion, by culture, so we don't notice that they are picking our pockets. That they are defunding our schools, that they are gutting our healthcare, that they are raising taxes on all of us while they cut taxes for themselves. It is the oldest strategy in the world, divide and conquer."],[978,"But tonight we sent a crystal clear message to the people at the top. We will not be conquered. I think it's safe to say that we are tired of being pitted against each other. We are tired of being told to hate each other. It has been 10 years of this kind of politics, politics as blood sport, politics as trolling and owning, politics as professional wrestling."],[1016,"It tears families apart. It ends friendships and it leaves us all feeling terrible all the time. People across the political spectrum are hungry for a different kind of politics. Not a politics of hate, not a politics of fear, not a politics of division, but a politics of love."],[1048,"My faith teaches me that love is the strongest force in the universe. Love is not passive. Love is not neutral. Love is not weak. Love requires that we stand between the bullies and the bullied. Love requires that we look evil in the eye and not blink. That kind of love has always been a threat to the powers that be. That kind of love is revolutionary. That kind of love is creative."],[1082,"Hate is predictable. Hate is boring. Hate can't lower our energy bills. Hate can't teach a child to read. Hate can't build a future. But what hate can't do, love can."],[1109,"Love can turn a student into a scholar. Love can turn a closet into a nursery. Love can turn an enemy into a friend. Love can turn a campaign into a movement. Love, love can heal what's broken in America. We can't defeat the politics of division with more division. We can't win that game. We have to change the game."],[1143,"In my experience, when you extend an open hand rather than a closed fist, you'll be surprised by who takes that hand. We didn't win this race by alienating our neighbors, or shaming our neighbors, or ridiculing our neighbors. We embodied a new kind of politics, a politics rooted in a deep love for our state, for our country, and most importantly, for all of our neighbors."],[1178,"We mobilized. We mobilized our 60,000 volunteers in every corner of the state, and together we delivered bottled water to Sand Branch, a community south of Dallas with no running water. We donated school supplies to an elementary school in El Cenizo, a small town on the border. We collected more than 20,000 pounds of groceries for families in Fort Worth who are struggling under the high cost of living."],[1209,"Before the world changes in ways you see on TV or read about in newspapers, the world changes person to person, neighbor to neighbor. In each moment when you choose to be kind, in each neighbor we choose to love, in each prayer that we save for someone who would not pray for us in return. This is how we won Texas. This is a win the size of Texas. And now we have a mandate the size of Texas."],[1257,"This election was about chasing a vision of what this state can be. Texas public schools that are the envy of the nation, a Texas economy that is second to none, and Texas families that are stronger and healthier than they've ever been before. It won't happen overnight, but a giant state deserves giant dreams. And we know how to get there. We must get big money out of our politics, so no billionaire or trillionaire can buy our elections."],[1303,"We must unrig this economic system that only benefits the top 1%. We must pass universal healthcare, so no one goes bankrupt just because they get sick. We must invest in our teachers and our students, so every underdog has a fighting chance. We must end these corrupt forever wars that are driving up prices and killing our great men and women in uniform."],[1342,"And we must heal the deep spiritual corruption at the root of all of these crises. We must bridge the divides between us and repair the ties that bind us. We forged a new kind of politics here in the Lone Star State, an answer to this decade of division."],[1368,"We showed that when working people come together across every dividing line, we can do extraordinary things. We won this race because people who are desperate for change now are going to get change."],[1390,"That old politics is dying and a new politics is being born through each of us, through every underdog, through every David against every Goliath, through every Texan who believed in our state and believed in this movement. Now the real work begins."],[1409,"2,000 years ago when the people at the top hurt his neighbors, that barefoot rabbi didn't stay in his room and pray. He walked into the seat of power and he flipped over the tables of injustice. As this movement heads to the seat of power, as we head to the United States Senate, we know what this moment requires of us. Texas, it's time to start flipping tables."]]},"ossoff":{"videoId":"fsoikoGhJW0","src":"supplied","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"the American people have rebuked the depravity, corruption, and incompetence of the failed lame duck President Donald J. Trump.","t":162}],"full":[[18,"Hello, Atlanta. Thank you, Georgia. Georgia, you did it."],[37,"And let me be the first to offer public congratulations to the governor-elect of the state of Georgia, Keisha Lance Bottoms."],[68,"To every volunteer who poured your heart and soul into this effort and everyone who chipped in so we could face down the dark money super PACs, thank you."],[83,"To Charlie Bailey and his crew at the strongest Democratic Party of Georgia in a generation, thank you. To my staff, to Ellen and Keenan and Ray and Miriam and Chandra and the best team in American politics, thank you."],[105,"To my wonderful wife, Alicia, and my daughters, Eva and Lila, my parents and my entire family, thank you for your unconditional love and support."],[117,"And to the people of the great state of Georgia for the trust you’ve invested in me to continue representing you in the United States Senate, thank you. Thank you."],[126,"Thank you. Now Georgia. Thank you. I love you too."],[149,"And listen. In sweeping and decisive victories, the American people have rebuked the depravity, corruption, and incompetence of the failed lame-duck president Donald J. Trump."],[180,"And if at times these last two years, amidst the ceaseless onslaught of brutality and indecency, you doubted whether our republic would survive. Let tonight’s results give you courage that the first light of dawn is on the horizon."],[205,"But remember that in living rooms and backyards and at rallies across Georgia these last two years, together, we’ve affirmed that our task is not just to contain one president’s wickedness, but to heal the brokenness beneath. That this moment is an opening not for restoration, but for reformation."],[229,"And so amidst our celebration tonight, we must acknowledge that the underlying crisis gripping our republic remains, and that therefore our most vital work lies ahead."],[246,"Because while the wealthy and well lobbied feast on inside information and official favors, America’s forgotten families are treated to systemic corporate disrespect and official indifference, working harder and harder while the treadmill just gets faster and steeper and the bills get higher and higher. Yes, sir."],[269,"Instead of reading your daughter her favorite book, that precious spare hour after work, you’re on the phone begging the insurance company to cover the medicine that prevents her seizures."],[282,"You report the black mold to your landlord who doesn’t fix the leak, and the ambulance for your toddler’s asthma attack is followed by a $3,000 bill. For too many, homeownership’s a fantasy. Family farms face ruin."],[null,"And while health care’s never cost more, plastics invade our bodies, blood and breast milk, toxic forever chemicals taint half the country’s drinking water, and polluters have been granted fresh license to poison our air."],[330,"Humanity is fast forgetting the terrible lessons of two world wars and the Holocaust. Meanwhile, the titans of Silicon Valley dig bunkers for themselves and warn that the artificial intelligence they’re creating risks human extinction."],[347,"And amidst these challenges of unprecedented consequence and complexity, though we rightly celebrate tonight’s historic victory, the fact is we’ve been too long mired in a small and selfish politics bought by big money, unmoored from fixed moral principles, and resigned to intractable division. In other words, the United States has been adrift in a gale."],[378,"But Georgia, we can and will reclaim control over our own destiny. Tonight, we’ve struck a necessary and undeniable blow on behalf of justice and progress."],[394,"And tonight in Georgia, we’ve proven not just that unity is possible, but that we can overcome division without sacrificing clarity of purpose."],[406,"In every corner of Georgia, this campaign urged the necessity of banning corporate and secret money from politics, of American leadership for peace and human rights around the world, and of guaranteeing health care for every single American."],[425,"We committed to continuing the work of bringing Big Pharma, big insurance, and Big Tech to heel in the defense of struggling Georgia families."],[433,"And on that basis, we built a new majority that extends far beyond party lines. And the foundation for that new majority has been trust."],[452,"Trust built through years of phone calls to mayors, pastors, and farmers. And trust measured in problems solved together without concern for ideology or party affiliation."],[465,"I thank Republican Mayors Matheson, Smith, and Fry of Valdosta, Tifton, and Toccoa, and the countless other Republican leaders who joined our team."],[473,"And I thank the hundreds of thousands of independent and Republican voters who joined our winning coalition. Never doubt that unity is possible."],[493,"Even in his final months, Congressman Lewis always reminded us that we all live in “one American house.” Do you remember? In “one world house.”"],[505,"He called it the inevitable truth that we’re all members of one human family."],[512,"And I know many of you have poured yourselves into this campaign, not for my sake or for the sake of a Democratic Party, but because you’re so deeply troubled by the pain our fellow human beings are enduring right now."],[527,"The terror of a child watching ICE take away her mother. The despair of a cancer patient losing coverage mid-treatment. But that ache in your heart, that pit in your stomach, that feeling is what reminds us we’re all in this together."],[null,"Yes, sir. That we’re not just one United States. We’re one united people. “E pluribus unum.” “Out of many, one.”"],[560,"And over centuries, despite our sins and through courageous struggle, the flame of American freedom has grown brighter and bolder and given hope to the whole world."],[571,"We’ve stumbled. We almost lost our way."],[578,"But Georgia, for all our troubles, let me assure you tonight that propelled by this historic and undeniable victory, I have no doubt we will overcome them."],[595,"And now our task is to reawaken that great national spirit that defeated fascism and established Social Security, that put men on the moon and passed civil rights laws in order to meet the challenges and obligations of our time."],[610,"Because I refuse to accept that my two little girls will grow up in a world as dark and dangerous and cruel as this one threatens to become."],[619,"I refuse to accept that Eva and Lila will grow up with artificial friends and teachers in a society where the sick die, not because there’s no cure, but because they have no money. Where we have enough nuclear weapons to destroy the world a thousand fold, but we refuse to guarantee health care for every citizen. On a poisoned planet, rearming for world war, where human life is cheap and might makes right."],[null,"See, when Eva’s old enough to ask why I let this happen, I’m determined to answer truthfully that I didn’t."],[661,"I’ll tell her how the same year she turned five, Georgia overcame every doubt and dirty trick, not just to win, but to set a new course for our state and our country and our world."],[672,"That we defended voting rights and civil rights at home. That we restored American leadership toward peace and human rights around the world. That we finally acted to ban corporate money and secret money from our politics. And that we guaranteed health care for every single American."],[694,"Thank you, Georgia. Tonight, we celebrate this victory, and tomorrow, we get back to work. Thank you so much. Thank you, Georgia. Thank you."]]},"kiros":{"videoId":"z2eeF9dUctg","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"excerpts":[{"text":"Not the billionaires, not the corporations or the special interests, I'm fighting in Congress for you.","t":176}],"full":[[7,"482 days over 8,000 volunteers [cheering] 140,000 doors knocked and over 500,000 phone calls made. That is what it took to send a 29-year-old immigrant"],[38,"barista renter recovering lawyer and Democratic Socialist to Congress. Denver you did this. Quick show of hands, how many people in this room it was your first time volunteering for a campaign? Look at that. Look around this room."],[68,"This night belongs to every single one of you. I want to thank my parents [cheering] my sister my aunties, my uncles, my cousins, my friends [cheering] and all of the new friends that I've met along this way for being a part of this campaign. To Justice Democrats, to Denver DSA, the Working Families Party, Sunrise, to"],[100,"every single union and organization that supported this campaign, thank you. And to our organizing team, the greatest a girl could ever ask for. YOU JUST [screaming] MADE HISTORY. [cheering] My parents came to Denver from Ethiopia in '98 on a diversity visa lottery program. I was 11 months old. My parents"],[131,"started over from scratch, worked multiple jobs to put my my dad through pharmacy school at CU Denver, and they picked Denver because they knew we'd be welcome here. And tonight, Denver proved them right. [cheering] And that is the Denver that I am taking to Congress. A city A city where it doesn't matter if you've been here for decades or just days, whether you cross the border or the"],[161,"border crossed you. Whether you make $500,000 or $50,000, you belong here, and you deserve to live here with dignity and opportunity. Not the billionaires, not the corporations or the special interests, I'm fighting in Congress for you. [cheering] And I want to speak directly to the corporations, and the lobbyists,"],[192,"and the dark money groups who spent who spent millions of dollars to try and stop this campaign. I hate to break it to you, but you failed. You see, 20 people spent $2 billion this cycle in the midterms to try and stop us. That's just nationally."],[223,"Elon Musk alone spent almost $500 million. But here's the thing, no one knows better how fragile this system they've created is than the billionaires. No one knows better how powerful we all could be organized collectively than the billionaires. [cheering] That's why they spend this time, this"],[255,"money, these resources trying to keep us divided, trying to keep us atomized and hateful of one another. But this movement, this campaign proved that we know our collective POWER AND WE ARE COMING TO FIGHT BACK. [cheering] We won because our fight is righteous. We are fighting for a world where your paycheck actually covers your rent."],[287,"Where cancer diagnosis doesn't send you into bankruptcy. Where our immigrant neighbors don't have to live in fear of a big deadly rogue agency. WHERE OUR TAX DOLLARS ARE SPENT INVESTING in our babies here at home, not killing babies abroad. Where our Where our elected officials represent their voters, not their donors. That means"],[317,"That means we have to pass Medicare for all. WE HAVE TO PASS A LIVING WAGE FOR ALL. TO ABOLISH TO ABOLISH ICE. TO END [cheering] To end the endless genocidal wars. [cheering] AND TO FINALLY GET BIG MONEY OUT OF OUR POLITICS. That is what Denver voted for tonight."],[347,"And that is why I'm going to fight like hell for every single Denverite. [cheering] And let me And let me just say to the other candidates in this race who stepped up to serve their communities, to speak up for their own views and their own platforms. Thank you. Running is not easy. We need a hell of a lot more people stepping up to serve their communities."],[378,"And for anyone who voted for these candidates, we might not agree on everything. And in a healthy democracy, that's okay. But that won't stop me from fighting like hell for you. For you and your right to live freely and peacefully with dignity, regardless of your party, regardless of your faith, your gender, your orientation, your status, because the greatest lie that was ever told was that freedom that we're fighting for is scarce."],[408,"That the freedom is so scarce that there's only so much of it to go around, and that for some to hold it, others have to go without it. Freedom is not a fortune to be hoarded. It is a right. It is a right that no billionaire, nor corporation, no special interest could ever take away from us. That is the promise of this country, of the American dream. Not a dream that shrinks to fit the few, but one wide enough to hold all of us together."],[440,"[cheering] Because it is only together that we can truly achieve true liberation and freedom. This country belongs to everyone who loves what it stands for. The people born here, the people who just got here. Everyone who thinks democracy is worth defending and that every person is deserving of dignity. It is because of this fight for our"],[472,"collective freedoms that we won tonight. This is a movement. One that follows a long line of dreamers and fighters and giants whose shoulders we stand on tonight. And we are just getting started. [screaming] Thank you all so much for being here with us. Thank you all for celebrating this historic victory."],[513,"DENVER! TONIGHT YOU ARE SENDING THE FIRST Gen Z woman, the first black woman, and the first Ethiopian American to serve in United States Congress. I owe a lifetime of gratitude to every"],[543,"single one of you in this room, and I'm going to pay it back by"]]},"hamawy":{"videoId":"1tGUD7JciGk","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"note":"The transcript shows people being interviewed before the result was known. This video does not contain a speech by the candidate.","excerpts":[],"full":[[3,"It's historic because I'm going with someone who was [music] actually in Gaza and witnessed the genocide. So, I'm someone the first person there an eyewitness and there on the ground. It's historic as the first Muslim in New Jersey to get elected to Congress. And um it's historic win for the people just across the country as we see this wave of uh blue Democrats win over and over again. Do you think the Democrats will flip the house today? Absolutely. Why not? Uh absolutely. I think everybody knows it and it's going"],[33,"to happen. The signs look like the Democrats have a good chance of flipping the house. And makes me feel greatly relieved and uh renews my faith in our country. I think this election in 2026 compared to all the other ones we're going to get a lot of turnout all over the nation. If you look around, a lot of people are waking up. They're looking at what's going on in New York. They're looking at what's going on in Michigan. They're like, \"You know what? If they can do it, so can we.\" So, New Jersey, New York, Michigan, Texas,"],[65,"they're seeing what's going on within the certain populations. They're saying, \"Hey, we got to wake up.\" So, honestly, tonight's tonight where we're going to see a massive change within the United States of America. It's going to be for the better. Uh the win feels really incredible to be part of the campaign and help organize uh events within my town for Adam. Uh again, I just want people fighting for the working class uh for healthcare. We all deserve healthcare. I mean, for me it shows us that like, you know, dark money, uh super PAC money, and in general corporate funds"],[96,"can't win elections no more. That like the working class citizen and the working class everyday Joe uh can help and volunteer and we truly can make a difference and make a change in politics. Money can't buy everything. That like organized people can really beat organized money. Our work is not over. Basically, um after um Dr. Adam Hamdan uh inshallah like wins this uh general election, that the the work starts the next day because"],[128,"right now Gaza is still under siege, Gaza is still being bombed, and we need to bring this home. We need to bring this issue back into the headlines. Like we don't want our taxpayer money to be spent on war and genocide"]]},"powell":{"videoId":"4iNIoBXcFrw","src":"captions-auto","paras":true,"note":"This is a television news report announcing the result, not a speech by the candidate.","excerpts":[],"full":[[0,"First Alert 6 live at 10:00, Decision 2026 coverage continues with the big headline at this hour, Denise Powell victorious in the race to take over Republican Don Bacon's seat in CD2. So, not only is she the first Latina for Nebraska in Congress, but look at this. Only two women have been elected to the US House. Virginia Smith, a Republican, she served eight terms from 1975 to 1991. You can tell the history of this, she has a black and white photo, and now"],[31,"we can add Denise Powell to this list of women to elected to the US House. And also added to the five women of the history of Congress for Nebraska. Well, that does it for First Alert 6 live at 10:00 tonight for Decision 2026 coverage. We will have more when we come back."]]},"raman":{"videoId":"vquC7apsR90","src":"supplied","paras":true,"note":"This video is a press conference held the morning after the election, with questions from reporters. It is not an election-night speech.","excerpts":[{"text":"I'm an immigrant to this country.","t":215},{"text":"to make people believe in Los Angeles again","t":255}],"full":[[0,"All right, good evening everyone. Um, I just wanted to say how grateful I am for the trust that Angelos have placed in me uh to be their next mayor. It was a hard-fought campaign. It was many, many months in the making. People from across this city welcomed me into their backyards, into their neighborhoods, told me about their hopes and dreams for the future of this city and trusted in me that I would be able to take on the problems that we have."],[33,"I'm also so incredibly grateful to the thousands of volunteers that knock on doors, make phone calls, send texts, talk to their neighbors, talk to their families, talk to their friends to tell them about a vision for Los Angeles that looks different, more hopeful than the one that we have today. Woohoo! [cheering] Wanted to express [applause] my deepest gratitude for Mayor Bath and her decades of service to the city. We had an opportunity to speak this morning and we both share a love for Los Angeles and her service, her decades of service in community coalition as a nurse in the emergency room, her decades of activism in South LA, her work in Sacramento, in DC, and as the first woman mayor of the city. All of this has made Los Angeles what it is today, an deeply, deeply inclusive place. To me, what is the the epitome of the American dream, a place that welcomes people, [cheering]"],[102,"[applause] a place that welcomes people and and invites them to build their dreams here, invites them to build their dreams here. And she helped build that dream here. And I know her service uh is something that people across America have gratitude for and certainly every person across Los Angeles. Uh we also committed to working together on the smoothest possible transition for Angelinos."],[127,"We love this city. We want to make it an incredible incredible place into the future and our staffs are already in touch to make sure that every aspect of this mayoral administration handoff is going to be as smooth as it needs to be in order to ensure that services for Angelinos are as good as they need to be. So, I want to thank you all for being out here and um I'm here today because you know this morning was when the news was confirmed and I'm here with my staff both from my council office and my campaign just to share a few moments of gratitude and togetherness. So, and I want to thank all of you for being up here as well."],[171,"[applause] Can you describe Can you describe [applause] Can you describe the the emotions of this? Can you describe the emotions of this moment of of actually having this confirmed? When you look around and you see your staff, you think about the fact that you are now going to be the mayor of Los Angeles. [cheering] [applause] This city has given me and my family so much. And at a time when in the federal government over the past two years, we've seen a country that has rejected immigrants and And in so many ways they immigrant dream. I'm an immigrant to this country."],[219,"And this is a city of immigrants in so many ways. Whether they came from across America or whether they came from across the world. This city has opened its arms to people to come and build their dreams here. And the idea that Angelinos voted for an immigrant to be their next mayor at this moment in American history is so deeply moving to me. And I want to tell every single Angelino out there, I am going to work so hard. Everyone behind me is going to work so hard to earn your trust. Your trust [applause]"],[255,"everyone across the city to make people believe in Los Angeles again, to make people believe in it city hall again. [cheering] Public [applause] safety is top of mind for a lot of people right now. Police union put out a statement today saying that there are LAPD officers and others who are filled with angst and uncertainty at the prospect of major cuts to LAPD. Will there be major cuts to LAPD? And do you still plan to fire police chief Jim McDonald?"],[289,"You know, I have spoken to leadership at LAPD already. In fact, I I'm um speaking to Chief McDonald. I spoke to him earlier today. It was one of the first calls that I made because public safety is the most important service that the city is delivering to its people. It is hands down the most important service. What about and and I want to make sure that whatever happens over this transition that we are prepared to deliver that service at the level that Angelinos expect when I take office in mid December. And I know Chief McDonald committed to that. I'm committed to that. We'll continue those discussions."],[326,"Mayor, like what is sort of maybe your first 100 day plan? Have you started to develop a sort of checklist of the first things you want to do like on day one per se? You know, we have published a 100 days plan during the campaign. I will say that in the few hours between when this election results were confirmed and now I have mostly taken congratulatory phone calls and spoken to people and just tried to ensure that our transition is ready to go. We have 40 days to build this transition. It's one of the shortest transitions across the country."],[361,"For a city of 4 million people where the challenges are absolutely immense, that transition is going to be absolutely critical. And so today's work was about kickstarting that transition with the skills, the people, and the priorities that we need to make sure that our first 100 days are successful. That was what today was about. And and when we have more to announce about what that transition looks like and what the first 100 days will look like, we will share that with you. What are you going to say to the voters for you? Okay."],[389,"What are you going to do? to work with acknowledged full council members membership that is not on your side. You know, I spoke to many of my council colleagues already today and I'll continue speaking to them in the in the days ahead and with every single person the conversation was absolutely the same. Uh, congratulations on to me and my commitment to them, our shared commitment to working together for the betterment of this city. No matter what happened during the campaign, that is in the past now. And all of us, every single member of that city council and I are here because we love Los Angeles and we know that we need to work together in order to address the challenges that we have ahead. And every conversation was about making that commitment to one another and to the people of the city."],[441,"We will work together to make it better. The three main points when you come to city hall, the three main points when you come to city hall, what are your three main points when you come to city hall to work? You know, we we have um the key priorities that we've heard across this entire city are homelessness, housing costs, and public safety. and economic health. These are the issues that are the four top issues on the minds across every neighborhood where whether you were in Studio City, whether you were in Silar, whether you in San Pedro, whether you in Wilmington, whether you're in Royal Heights. These are the four key issues that came up over and over again. These are the priorities that I take on in city hall and we will have more plans to share as we are question four million people."],[495,"Yes. Didn't vote for you or didn't vote at all. What is your message? Yes. So, um I know many many people across the city voted for Mayor Bass or simply didn't participate in this election at all. And I think that's a sign of the deep distrust and cynicism that has taken hold here in the city of Los Angeles. My goal is to earn your trust. My goal is to make sure that we're doing the work to actually have a city hall that is capable of delivering on the promises that I made during the campaign. That's what this transition is about. That's what the next few weeks are about. That's what my first 100 days will be about. We have big challenges here in the city and they've been in place for a long time. What we have not had in the city hall that is capable of taking them on. That's a promise I made during the campaign is that we will build that city hall. That is my commitment to every single person."],[550,"Whether you voted for me or you didn't or you sat out this election completely, I want to make sure that we can restore your faith in city hall again. [cheering] [https\\://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/6/city-of-immigrants-who-is-nithya-raman-the-los-angeles-mayor-elect]("]]}},"extra":[{"key":"sand","name":"Rob Sand","eyebrow":"Additional speech · Iowa governor’s race","videoId":"Vb6ZaCH53vI","title":"FULL | Rob Sand delivers victory speech in 2026 Iowa governor's race","channel":"We Are Iowa Local 5 News","full":[[14,"Thank you, Iowa. Thank you, Iowa. I love you, Iowa. We got a family up here of Republicans and Democrats and Independents. I want to first thank my wife, Christine, and our two boys, Tate and Axel. For your support and for the sacrifices that you shared in our effort. I, I couldn't have done it without you, truly. Uh, Christine, you've, you've carried a weight. You've offered helpful advice."],[46,"You deserve just as much credit for this as I do. My parents My parents, Leslie and Kevin, my sister Jen, my in-laws, Nix, your help was invaluable in deciding which tie to wear for the third debate. Thank you for that. Really appreciate that. Uh, Aggie, thank you for being my bill, and, uh, most importantly, Walter, rest in peace. The energy and the excitement that He brought to the campaign was irreplaceable."],[80,"Christine said something profound the other day. She had been bracing for a difficult October, and, uh, yet everything that we imagined it would be was nothing compared to how hard it has been losing Walter. There are countless other. Family members and friends who have been with me every step of the way. It's been a long 18 months on the campaign trail, and I could not have gotten here without your support. You know who you are. Thank you."],[111,"Thank you To my running mate and Iowa's next lieutenant governor Dave Muhlbauer. We love Dave, don't we? I love this guy. When I asked him to join the ticket, we were actually at his mom's house with his mom. I looked around the house and I could tell that he had the same kind of upbringing that I did, uh, raised by good people with good values, same kinds of sayings on the wall, same kinds of decoration."],[157,"And I gotta say, anyone who can get elected in a county that goes 75% for the other party in the race for president has to be a peacemaker and a public servant. Amen for that. Literally no wonder why we had multiple. Republican elected officials who endorsed me just because I picked Dave. I hadn't talked to them. I hadn't called them. I hadn't asked for their endorsement. They just saw that I picked Dave Mbauer and they're like, well, me too then. Yeah."],[193,"So we got a good one here, Iowa, a really good one. He brings along a great family too. Thank you to, uh, Linda as well and the kids for letting Dave help me get here today. Very excited for our partnership ahead and to have his work ethic, especially added to serve Iowans. Thank you to Republican and independent public endorsers of this campaign for your courage and for your leadership genuinely."],[224,"We do live in a broken two choice political system where it requires real listening to learn that a candidate that is in the other party doesn't see you as the enemy. You listened. You knew that you would receive some negative reaction for endorsing across party lines, but you knew that the angriest ones are the loudest. And you knew that you were willing to stand publicly on principle to support returning our state to balanced government."],[255,"We have to have, we have to have bigger hearts and minds than just our party. And everyone who did that across party lines with a public endorsement showed that, and we thank you for it. To Iowa Democrats. You've had a hard few years here in Iowa. But balanced government has been restored. You stayed strong, you worked hard. So many of you feel what I feel about the divisiveness of our political system, and you were excited to have somebody as a candidate in your party who was actually talking about that and focusing on it."],[313,"But even among those of you that. Don't like that part as much. Well, the vast majority of you understood that the smallest party has to appeal to reasonable minded people in other parties if it wants to build a coalition that reaches a majority, because of all of us coming together in January, no Iowan has to fear their government anymore. To those who did not vote for me, I'm going to listen to you and serve you just the same."],[351,"I hope you already know that I had senior leaders in the auditor's office who were an independent and a Republican who had made campaign contributions to my opponent in 2018. I'm going to continue a similar approach. I hope if you see me out and about in our state, I mean, I'm going to be out and about. And I know that there's plenty of Iowans who did not vote for me, so you are gonna see me out and about."],[372,"I hope that you stop me, and I hope you introduce yourself, and I hope you kindly tell me why you didn't vote for me. I hope you also keep an open mind. Because you're gonna get to know me better over the next 4 years, and maybe you'll feel differently the next time. Bottom line is this. Again, for the folks who didn't vote for you, for me, I'm gonna work just as hard for you as I do for anyone else. Thank you also for voting and for being hard."],[404,"Appreciate that. Now, given that we are here tonight, Democrats and Independents and Republicans together, as we did at 200 town halls and countless rallies across this state, who is gonna start us in singing America the Beautiful? Oh, you know what? Hold on. Did we, we didn't have anybody go yet, right? All right, I'm gonna step aside and just so that we have a clear note and one person that we can all join in, Virginia will start us off."],[440,"the Just uh. Tonight Iowans sent a clear message. They want government not to work for a few one-siders or special interests or for one party, but for all Iowans. From the beginning of this campaign, it's been about being something bigger than Democrats versus Republicans. It's been about our shared yearning. To be one with our neighbors, and it's about speaking that indisputable truth that our leaders, like most of us, should be seeking in Iowa that isn't redder or bluer, but better and truer."],[524,"It's been about returning to our proud and long-standing Iowa tradition of balanced government. That we do our best work when we're forced to work together. I actually heard a Democratic and Republican legislative leader around 2013. Say just exactly that. We do our best work when we're forced to work together. Come January, we will be forced to work together. That teamwork That teamwork, if we are one as a state, is only natural left wing."],[566,"Right wing Same bird When Iowa Democrats and Iowa Republicans and Iowa Independents send their kids off to school in the morning, They don't tell them be red or be blue. We all tell them the same thing. Be good Do your best Tell the truth. It's as simple as that. It's time that we focus on the values that we share, not on the things that we divide us. This campaign has also been about returning us to our tradition of leading in good government reforms."],[603,"Iowa, first state to create a redistricting commission that was independent from politics and a judicial nomination system. Based on merit and the opinions of ordinary Iowans, we should now return to that tradition. We should be among the first states to end the special legal privileges of the Democratic and the Republican parties, and the system that enables the lesser of two evils, and lead elected officials not into the temptation of politics, but down the straight and narrow path of public service rather than politics."],[644,"These ideas didn't just win, they resonated. They didn't just resonate, maybe they caught fire. I want to thank the Iowans from across the state and across the political spectrum who not only voted for me but also got involved, donated, volunteered, had conversations with people in their lives about the movement that we've been building. We saw unprecedented support from across the aisle throughout this campaign."],[668,"Literally thousands of registered Iowa Republicans and thousands of registered Iowa independents who didn't just vote for me but donated to this campaign. We had over 117,000 donors to this campaign chipping in an average of $155. Many of you are here tonight. Thank you again. We also heard countless stories from first-time voters in their 30s or 40s getting off the sidelines to vote for the first time in this race."],[701,"Doesn't happen overnight, doesn't happen by accident. It happens when people who have felt ignored for the last decade, who have lost all faith in their elected officials or in state government. Or who have struggled to get by while watching politicians work to make life harder for them, finally feel heard and seen and recognized, and finally hearing someone say the thing that they think about our political system."],[729,"Over the course of 200 public town halls, that's exactly what this campaign did. We gave Iowans a place to bring their concerns, their complaints, and their ideas to improve our state. We rejected the idea that you have to hate your neighbor just because they vote differently than you, and we said that we should expect more from our elected officials who are supposed to be working for us."],[749,"That is what this campaign has been about. Now it's going to take all of us working together from all political persuasions to address the issues that our state faces. But I truly believe that we can do great things for this state with all ideas, voices, and perspectives actually at the table. Politics should never, ever, ever be about two private clubs who are more interested in beating up on each other than they are in solving our problems."],[782,"Problem solving across the aisle is something that you can expect from me as your governor. My mission is going to be to make state government work better for all Iowans, to serve all Iowans, and to be accountable to all Iowans. We also learned something else in this campaign. The lies didn't work. The only two fair attacks about me were that I can ride a skateboard and I do like pizza."],[810,"And as Christine said, these lies were nothing compared to our loss on October 15th, but they're also nothing compared to the struggle that so many Iowans go through every single day, trying to provide for their families or play the difficult hand that they've been dealt in life. Enough Iowans know me well enough that they spread the truth to others around them about who I am, and that proved."],[834,"That Iowa can still work like one big small town where being open and being honest is the best way to get through it all in the end. Here's to Iowa on that one. I do want to thank my opponent, Zach Lane for getting in the race. I said the same thing when Governor Reynolds announced her retirement. Public office and campaigning is a difficult thing to do in a way that few people truly understand. Putting your name out there and your ideas out there is tough."],[865,"And I appreciated the places where we agreed. I'm glad to see someone win a Republican nomination talking about water quality and talking about cancer. Yeah. So let's use that bipartisan support from Iowa voters to actually get our water cleaned up and our cancer rates under control. Tonight Iowans across the state made their voices heard, and they voted to restore our public schools to their former glory."],[897,"They voted to address our cancer crisis with real solutions, not with rhetoric, and to make public service the focus of government, not politics, by regulating, well, the people that need regulation the most, politicians. More than anything else, Iowans voted for change. They voted for checks and balances, and they voted to bring transparency and accountability back to state government."],[924,"Now, to Iowa's legislators, I look forward to working with you on the same common sense ideas and solutions that we advocated for throughout this campaign. Iowans, including Democrats and Independents, voted for these issues. They are broadly popular, and we would all do well to pass them into reality. As I said on the campaign trail, I'm going to be spending 100% of my time addressing the concerns of 100% of Iowans, and you have my word, legislators, any bill you vote for is a bill where you are invited to the bill ceremony signing ceremony."],[960,"That's the kind of credit given where credit is due, sort of common sense attitude that Iowans expect from their government. Thank you again. To the people of the state of Iowa for putting your trust in me as your next governor. I hope. And I hope No matter who you voted for in this race. I hope over the next week, you're going to go find somebody that voted differently than you and ask them why, and just listen."],[995,"And keep asking, tell me more or say something else until they say something. That you agree with When they do that, Let them know. Will we agree on that. That's one thing that you can do yourself, everyone in the state to help rebuild the social fabric of our state, and remember that all of us together, our neighbors, our friends, we all have a job to do to make this state better and truer, not just redder and bluer."],[1025,"Let's get to work."]],"paras":true},{"key":"pingree","name":"Hannah Pingree","eyebrow":"Additional speech · Maine","videoId":"QzjdBiuZPe0","title":"‘Hard And Ugly Year In Politics’: Hannah Pingree's Fiery Victory Speech Draws Roars From Crowd","channel":"Hook Global","full":[[0,"Thank you, Maine. [cheering] Wow. Wow. Thank you all for being here. This is big. Really big. [cheering] [applause] I just want to start by saying that um I've gotten a phone call from Rick Bennett and from Bobby Charles to concede. [cheering] [cheering] You guys are fired up. Thank you. Thank you. [cheering] I don't know if you guys have been watching TV, but we're winning everywhere across this country."],[60,"[cheering] We've elected some incredible women governors in all these states. They didn't expect us to win. [cheering] Well, I before I say anything else, I need to say something to my amazing and competitive daughter, [laughter] Elsie. A little more than a year and a half ago, when we were debating as a family whether or not I should run, she looked at me and she said, \"You should do it, Mom, but you better win."],[103,"[cheering] We did it. We won. [cheering] [cheering] You told me. Jason, Elsie, Oscar, you gave up so much for this. family dinners, weekends, a mom often on the road. You did a great job having to talk to lots and lots of people. You starred in not one but two campaign ads. They did a great job. He really did make that basket on the first shot. [cheering] But she's better at basketball."],[152,"[laughter] I love you three more than words can say. Also to my mom, congrats on your victory tonight. [cheering] [applause] My mom has blazed a trail since she first won uh her race for tax assessor on North Haven when I was a little kid. to my dad, to my sisters Cesaly and Ava, my brother Asa, my amazing in-laws, all my nieces and nephews, my extended family, to my friends, to my amazing community on North Haven and all across Maine. Thank you."],[197,"[cheering] [applause] I do mean that in the deepest way I know how. To the volunteers who knocked on doors weekend after weekend and made calls on their lunch breaks. To the people who marched in parades, invited their neighbors to the living rooms and backyards. To the county and state committees and organizers who ensured that we competed in every single county all across this state."],[227,"[cheering and applause] to my staff who gave this campaign everything. [cheering] [applause] They are all amazing. I could not have asked for a better team. This v victory belongs to every single one of us. Every bit of it. I do again want to thank my opponents. To my four fellow primary opponents, we ran a positive, respectful campaign and I'm grateful for their support and their friendship. [cheering]"],[266,"[applause] I just got a a big hug upstairs from my friend Troy Jackson. I'm feeling good. [cheering and applause] And again to my two opponents in the general election, we had a few disagreements, sometimes loudly, but I want to thank them for stepping forward for their service to this country and to the commitment they all have to this state that we all love. [applause] Tonight, I also want to speak directly to everyone who voted for someone else."],[306,"I hear you. I respect you. And I will work just as hard for you as I will those who voted for me. Because this isn't about who voted for who. It is about what we can accomplish together. [cheering] [applause] I want to talk about what this night means. It's not about me. It is about all of us. It is about our future. Over 17 months, we traveled to every single corner of the state. We gathered on farms in Arus County, at a union hall in Scaggan, a boatyard in Rockport, the VFW hall in Farmington. We sat down in small businesses with homebuilders. We listened to students and seniors. We visited schools, hospitals, miltowns, even a future lobster processing plant."],[361,"And everywhere I went, I heard the same worries. Maine people worried about the rising cost of everything. Worried about making it through this winter and keeping their homes warm. Worried about whether their kids will be able to afford a home and build a life here. And worried about the future of the country that we all love. And yet I saw Maine people stepping up again and again for each other."],[386,"Neighbors banking firewood so nobody in town goes cold. business owners and clergy standing up for their immigrant neighbors. [cheering] [applause] I saw moms fighting to keep their local maternity ward open. Families banding together to buy their mobile home parks. Nobody told them to do this. They just did it because that is what we do in Maine for each other. Right. [applause]"],[424,"So, I grew up on an island, as you've heard, 12 miles off the coast of Rockland, where you learn early that nobody is coming to rescue you. You have to dig in and figure out how to solve problems together. When devastating winter storms hit our local boatyard, half the town showed up with tools and chains and baked goods. That is not a political philosophy. It's how Maine people care for each other. And tonight, Maine voted for that spirit. They voted for neighbors over noise. For [cheering]"],[459,"[applause] they voted for people who will do the work over people who want to divide us. I know a lot of folks in this room are tired and across the state of Maine, they're tired of politics. They're tired of chaos and fear. And I know this has been a hard and ugly year in politics. So many people are anxious about what's happening in Washington and what comes next. But I want to hear you. I want you to hear me say this. You were right to care so much. Your worry was never wasted. Tonight, we turned our worry into something big and important all across this country. Not just for Maine, but for all of us."],[503,"[cheering] [applause] So, let's talk about the work ahead. It starts right now. We ran on three things, and I'm going to wake up every morning and focus on them. Housing so that young families can afford to stay here in the state of Maine. [cheering and applause] health care that's close to home that you can afford and that we can actually figure out how to navigate. [applause]"],[540,"Strong communities with good jobs where small businesses can thrive, where kids have great public schools, where all mayors feel safe and protected, and where we're ready for the storms ahead. So, none of this is going to be easy. There are no magic fixes, especially as the legislators in the front of the room know. [laughter] I spent 25 years in public service, and here's what I've learned. Big things happen when people stay focused. When you bring people together, even people who don't always agree, and we refuse to give up until the job is done. That is how I will govern. I'll work with Democrats, Republicans, independents, tribal leaders, local officials, unions, business owners, nurses, [cheering]"],[586,"teachers, loggers, fishermen. [applause] If you've got a good idea, my door will be open. And if someone threatens our people, our rights, or our state, I will stand up and fight. I will not back down. [cheering] [cheering] [applause] [cheering] Fire it up. [cheering] [cheering] [cheering] You all know we can stand firm for our values and stand up for our neighbors and we can still roll up our sleeves and get things done. That is the main I know. A place where common sense and hard work still matters. Where we look out for one another. Where we don't give up when things are hard. So I spent a lot of time thinking about my kids and your kids. I think about whether they will be able to afford to build a life here, whether they'll feel safe and hopeful about the future, whether they will inherit a democracy that works, a healthy planet, communities where neighbors still look out for each other."],[674,"I believe that they will. Not because any of that is guaranteed, but because of what I have seen main people, what we can do when we get together and decide to make things happen. So, tonight is actually about celebrating. We've earned it. You got to hug somebody, text your mom. We've all earned it. And then we're going to get to work. So, tonight is not the the finish line. It is the starting line. So, I'm asking you all to stay with me, to keep showing up, to keep believing what we can accomplish together. So, question. Are you with me?"],[719,"[cheering] [applause] [cheering] [screaming] [applause] [cheering] We have fought hard these last months for each other. We believed Maine's future was worth the fight. So now we're going to get to work building that future together. So one more time, are you with me? [cheering] I just want to say thank you Maine. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you everyone. All"]],"paras":true},{"key":"james","name":"Letitia James","eyebrow":"Additional speech · New York State Attorney General","videoId":"Fv4yPiRraHU","title":"New York State Attorney General Letitia James delivers victory speech","channel":"WGRZ-TV","full":[[0,"Please welcome to the stage your New York State Attorney General, Letitia James. -- Stop -- me, I'm Ah. Thank you so much. I wanna thank all of you who are here. Thank you so much for your support. I wanna thank my family that's somewhere out there, my nephew Ronald, my niece Robin, my other niece Laila, my great niece. Yes, that's me, that's Jamani Williams. He just did that because he wanted to be recognized, ah."],[57,"And I of course want to thank the labor. All of the unions that are here in the audience right now. 8:31 baby. Uh, that's why we have a middle class because of the labor movement. I thank you. My heart is full tonight. The victory belongs to each and every one of you, from Long Island to the hills of the Catskills, from the Hudson Valley to the lake shore of Rochester, from the Finger Lakes to Buffalo and to the streets of New York City."],[101,"And everywhere in between for nearly 8 years with the aid of so many in this room and across our state, we have used the sword and the shield of the law to protect the rights of New Yorkers, no matter what God they worship, no matter what the color of their skin, no matter their gender or who they love, no matter their immigration status or their socioeconomic status. Because our state has always defined itself by the diversity of our strength and the strength of our diversity, and we are all in this together."],[140,"And so for nearly 8 years we fought for every New Yorker without fear or without favor, and tonight New Yorkers told us loud and clear they want Tish James to finish the job. I, I ran for office because I saw my neighbors, hardworking, kind, and capable. They were left out of the sunshine of opportunity, and those same neighbors, no matter what office I hold or what cause I serve, they remain my North Star."],[179,"But these days, powerful forces are urging us to leave, leave our neighbors behind. apart, pulling us apart and pitting one group against the other, national leaders who peddle cruelty and call it policy. Those who traffic in fear and call it authority. But as we learned tonight and down the ballot, New Yorkers will not stand for leaders like that. They rejected their fear mongering."],[210,"In New York, we love our neighbors. We share both the burden and the fruit, and when someone needs help, we lend our hand. I know those values that New Yorkers hold because I see it on the streets of New York City. I see it across the state. I see it in my church. I see it in the communities across the state. I saw it on Marathon Sunday. We are community. We are the people. These values are reflected in the scriptures that I read, the values that define me, inform me, and so I and we will continue to stand up, fight back, and defend our values as ballots continue to be counted."],[262,"We're going to change the direction of this nation. We're going to course correct and my good friend, Congressman Hakeem Jeffries. is set to wield the Speaker's gavel to lead from the front and not the back. It's been the honor of my life to serve as Attorney General, and I will be forever grateful for every moment that I am here to serve and defend the interests of New York. And so I just wanted to thank all of you."],[295,"I wish you well, and I'll see you very soon as I continue the work of the Office of the Attorney General in the state of New York. All"]],"paras":true},{"key":"omar","name":"Ilhan Omar","eyebrow":"Additional speech · U.S. Representative, Minnesota","videoId":"ajiZs6uob40","title":"Rep. Ilhan Omar delivers victory speech","channel":"KARE 11","full":[[12,"I love you too. How are you all doing DFLers? It is an incredible election night results that we are seeing here in Minnesota and across the country. This is what it looks like when we lead with compassion, empathy, and courage. This is what it looks like when you give a damn about your neighbors. And this is what it looks like when you go out and you vote your values. Because when this administration came for Minnesotans, we knew that we could respond by showing up in the streets and protecting our neighbors, but we also knew when election day came that we were going to provide an answer."],[77,"Answer by directly rejecting them in the ballot box. That with every vote we get to tell them that Minnesota is not the place you mess with. I was telling folks earlier. That couple of weeks ago when they decided that they were going to come for me. They thought that they were going to find someone who was going to cower they thought they were going to find a community that was going to live in fear they thought that if you attacked me and you silenced me that my community wouldn't show up and vote."],[134,"And in Minnesota. We have shown people that we can vote and we can vote big. But I also wanna give a shout out to every community that he has attacked that has responded with a resounding rejection of his candidates that's Ohio. That's Maine. That is Texas. Because what we are seeing tonight, it is about telling this administration, it's about telling the bigot in the White House and his friends."],[182,"That we are not going to be a pawn in their game. So thank you Minnesota. Thank you for welcoming my family when we came here as refugees. Thank you for giving us. A chance at a new life. Thank you for helping educate me and my sisters and brothers, thank you for giving my father the opportunity to retire with dignity. And thank you for reminding this nation that you didn't just welcome a young refugee, but you chose her and sent her to Congress."],[242,"Tonight we get to celebrate our win. Because we worked for this win. Yes, and tomorrow we get to help make our trifecta work for us in creating progress. I will, I will, I will end with this. My colleague from California, the soon to be chairman of the oversight committee, Robert Garcia. Was asked. What he thought about our victory and what message he had for Trump and his allies, and he said you better lawyer up."],[308,"Because your time of harassment is over, it is our time for accountability and transparency. And if you thought that the Democrats took it easy on you in 2019, wait until you meet these kind of new Democrats. Thank you and I love you all. Al"]],"paras":true},{"key":"kiros-9news","name":"Melat Kiros","eyebrow":"Additional speech · Colorado’s 1st District","videoId":"I0wTM8eI3Kk","title":"Melat Kiros speaks after being elected to Congress","channel":"9NEWS","full":[[3,"Congratulations to this entire slate to Governor-elect Phil Weiser, to Lieutenant Governor-elect Leslie Dahlf, to Jeff Bridges, to Jenna Griswold, Amanda Gonzalez. Congratulations to my new colleagues in the delegation, Michael Bennett, John Hickenlooper, Joan Nagoose, Jason Crowe, Brittany Peterson. Incoming congressperson elect Mandy Ruinow. And y'all were up everywhere else."],[37,"I want to thank Congresswoman Diana DeGt for her 30 years of service to our city. She gave her career to this district that I'm grateful to follow in her steps and the steps of the late great Congresswoman Pat Schroeder as the 3rd woman and the first black woman to represent this incredible district. I'm a new member of this delegation and I'm also the youngest. I'm gonna. I'm gonna learn a lot from the people in this delegation who've been in these buildings longer than I have, and I plan to ask a lot of questions, but I'm also gonna stay true to what Denver sent me to do."],[86,"Working people are tired and they are angry. Rent eats over half of our paychecks. Energy bills keep going up. Premiums go up every year, and no one trusts Washington to get anything done. We earn that trust back by showing them who we work for and by delivering so let's be clear about what this party believes we believe that everyone deserves a home they can afford. We believe that no one should go bankrupt because they got sick."],[128,"We believe your vote should count just as much as a billionaire's. And we believe that Colorado belongs to everyone here whether you crossed the border or the border crossed you. I will not pretend that the work ahead will be easy. The future that we are reaching for is vast, even more vast than the injustices that it is meant to answer. Healthcare as a right, a home as a foundation, not a reward."],[164,"Health care as a right, a home as a foundation, a government that answers to the voters, not the donors. These are not just policies to be passed but promises to be made, and promises of this size are not kept in a single moment but over years of labor by many hands against fierce resistance. Look at how hard they worked to repeal Obamacare. We must be fierce in our resistance."],[200,"But I take comfort in knowing, in remembering who we are. We live in the legacy of those who looked at the moon and decided it was close enough to touch, those who crossed oceans to break the back of fascism and hatred, those who turned prairie and steel into the greatest economy the world has ever known. None of that was handed to us. It was willed into being by ordinary people who refused to accept the world as it was and decided instead to fight for a world that could be."],[240,"And the crisis before us for all its weight is no act of nature. It is the sum of choices made by a powerful few in rooms most of us will never see. But what was chosen can be unchosen. What was built can be rebuilt, and there is no force on earth more powerful than a people who have finally decided they deserve better. Who here thinks that we deserve better. All right, then let's get to work."],[281,"Because when we fight. When we fight. When we fight. Damn straight. Let's get to work, Colorado. Thank you. Please welcome Congressman Brittany Peterson. Sync to video time All"]],"paras":true},{"key":"kiros-assembly","name":"Melat Kiros","eyebrow":"Additional video · campaign speech, Denver county assembly","videoId":"t8Nw_vXIC_c","title":"This is the speech that won us 63% of the vote at Denver county assembly.","channel":"Melat Kiros for Congress","note":"This is a campaign speech from before the election, not an election-night speech. The video title is the campaign’s own claim.","full":[[0,"My name is Mea Curos. I'm a lawyer. I'm a PhD [music] student. I'm a barista. And I'm an immigrant. [cheering] I moved to Denver. I immigrated to Denver in 98 when I was a baby from Ethiopia. I watched my parents work for years to navigate the immigration process. And after they earned their citizenship and chose their political party, I asked my dad, \"Why are we Democrats?\" And he didn't hesitate to tell me about [music] the Civil Rights Act, Social Security, Fair Labor laws."],[38,"This is the party that fights for the people. [cheering] [applause] But it didn't just happen overnight. The party didn't just wake up and decide to do the right thing. It was pushed by organizers, by dreamers, by people who refuse to accept the world as it was. And with everything at stake right now, it's on us to push the party again. [cheering] [screaming] And not just to fight back against Trump, but to fight for a better world."],[79,"[screaming] [cheering] What a world where your salary actually covers your basic needs. Where our taxes fund universal healthcare instead of jobs. When our leaders [cheering] their voters instead of their donors, yes, they don't want us to believe that a world like that is possible because there is far too much money to be made by keeping things exactly as they are. I am grateful to the congresswoman for her service. But for us to meet this moment, there has to be a change."],[120,"[cheering] Change that starts by electing leaders [music] who are unbought, unafraid to stand up to the billionaires and corporations who got us here in the first place. [cheering] I am the only candidate in this race who refuses [music] corporate pack money because I am not ready to represent money interest. I rise to represent you and every voter who wants to see their leaders called to abolish ICE, [screaming]"],[158,"to end [cheering] the genocidal wars that are funded by our tax dollars, [cheering] and to root out the corruption in our government once and for all. [cheering and applause] Every single breakthrough [music] this party has had was born out of the hearts of people in rooms just like this who dared to believe that a better world was possible. I [music] want to see a show of hands real quick. How many people here, this is your first caucus and assembly? Look at that."],[200,"Look at how many people are here in this room ready to make a change, to be a part of making that change. This is a movement that is out for and by [music] the people. And I am so grateful to stand by all of you and to fight alongside all of you to take back power for the working people. [cheering] My name is Ma Curos and it would be my greatest honor to [music] serve as your next congresswoman. [cheering]"],[235,"[cheering] [music] [cheering] [cheering] A"]],"paras":true},{"key":"kiros-news","name":"Melat Kiros","eyebrow":"Additional video · Colorado’s 1st District","videoId":"vJ2jpSMqQBc","title":"Democratic Socialist Melat Kiros Makes History Winning Colorado's 1st Congressional District","channel":"Denver7","note":"This is a television news report, not her speech. Her speeches are on her profile card and in the cards just before this one.","full":[[2,"SEN THE RACE FOR SECRETARY OF STATE WITH ABOUT 6 STORTONIGHT, I GUESS WAS THE BIGGEST STORY PRIMARY NIGHT, BUT IT'S OFFICIAL TONIGHT. DEMOCRATIC SOCIALISTS OF AMERICA WINDS IN COLORADO THIS EVENING MAY LIKE HEROES HAS BEEN ELECTED TO ESENT COLORADO'S FIRST CONGRESSIONAL DISTRICT CARROLL'S WON TONIGHT'S RACE BY A LANDSLIDE.C >> JESSICA PORTER: NUMBER 7 ACR ELECTION HEADQUARTERS. WHAT A NIGHT, MICHAEL, FOR THIS. 29 YEAR-OLD."],[33,"YET, JESSICA AND SHANNON MAY LIKE HEROES IS MAKING A LOT OF HISTORY. FIRST, I JUST WANT TO RECOGNIZE THAT THE PARTY STILL VERY GOING STRONG HERE AT HEROES HEADQUARTERS, HER RACE WAS CAUGHT ABOUT 15 TO 20 MINUTES AFTER THE POLLS CLOSED, BUT HER SUPPORTERS ARE STICKING AROUND OUT SAYS VERY MUCH BEEN POLITICAL OUTSIDER BY MANY, BUT SHE BURST ONTO THENE EARLIER THIS YEAR. AND AS YOU MENTIONED IN JUNE, SHE FEED 30 INCUMBENT DIANA TO GET CONGRESSWOMAN DIANA TO GET AND SHE SAYS SHE IS NOW WITH THIS. SECUTHIS VICTORY, READY TO GET TO WORK. SHE SAYS SOME OFFIRST THING SHE WANTS TO DO IS REVERSE THE CUTS TO MEDICAID AND MEDICARE AS WELL AS THE TAX CUTS GIVEN TO THE WEALTHY. THIS MAKES HEROES WITHIS. WHEN THE FIRST BLACK CONGRESSWOMAN THE FIRST GEN Z AND AGAIN, THE FIRST DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST TO REPRESENT COLORADO IN CONGRESSEURO SHORTLY AFTER WINNING HET ONE ON ONE INTERVIEW. WHAT THIS REPRESENTATIONS IN TERMS OF REPRESENTING ALL OF THESE DIFFERENT PARTS OF HERSELF AND SO MANY COMMUNITIES."],[101,"AND IT HAS. I DID THWE ARE BETTER. >> MICAH SMITH: NOW AFTER THAT ONE ON ONE INTERVIEW, I SO WITNESSED LY INTERESTING MOMENT BETWEEN HEROES AND DENVER'S FIRST BLACK MAYOR WELLINGTON WEBB, 2 HERE IN THE DENVER AREA, BREAKING BARRIERS AND REPRESENT 2 VERY DIFFERENT GENERATIONS, BUT MAKING HISTORY NONETHELESS. NOW I ASK YOUR U.S. MORE ABOUT WHAT SHE PLANS TO DO AS SOON AS SHE GETS TO CONGRESS AS WELL AS WHWOULD SUPPORT FOR SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE WILL HAVE ALL OF MORE OF THAT ONE-ON-ONE INTERVIEW FOR YOU IN THE COMING DAYS. BUT FOR NOW REPORTING LIVE FROM HEROES HEADQU, MICAH SMITH, DENVER All"]],"paras":true}],"further":{"key":"mpu","videoId":"LYLPCXBKvvo","title":"What the Media is Missing About Democrats’ Midterm Victories","channel":"More Perfect Union","post":"https://substack.perfectunion.us/p/democrats-won-back-the-working-class","postLabel":"Democrats won back the working class (More Perfect Union post)","note":"The narration is by a More Perfect Union host and mixes in clips of candidates and commentators; bracketed names in the transcript mark who is speaking.","full":[[0,"To understand what happened in the midterm elections, take a look at this chart. Two years ago, Trump made his biggest gains where wages had fallen the most. In this election, low-income counties shifted Democratic by over 20 points. Republicans’ advantage in rural America shrank by double digits. So what happened? The media story is that Trump lost working people. That's true. But if you follow More Perfect Union, that's pretty obvious. On the surface, Democrats seem to be the party of the working class again."],[30,"The real fight in this country is not left versus right, it is top versus bottom. We showed that in a battle between the money and the many that the many really can win. In a politics dominated by billionaires and special interest groups, we will not bow down. [Faiz Shakir] But this movement could be either short-lived or durable. From what I've seen on the ground, in exit polls and in campaign spending, we'll discuss what could make this a political realignment rather than a reaction, and what Democrats could do right now to deliver on their biggest campaign promise: Affordability."],[71,"[Faiz Shakir] Here’s one more chart from data analyst G. Elliott Morris. It maps month by month how often members of Congress were using the defining word of this election. And it raises the question: What happened in mid-2025? At the time, during Trump's first year of his second term, two different visions were playing out within the Democratic Party. As Donald Trump and Elon Musk were torching government services... [Elon Musk] Chainsaw! [Faiz Shakir] ...firing government employees..."],[101,"[President Donald Trump] That’s not a job that’s going to make America great again. [Faiz Shakir] ...and courting the nation’s elite, one faction of the Democratic Party said, play dead, do nothing. [James Carville] My point is, just lay back. Play possum. And arose a different faction within the Democratic Party, the economic populists who said, “Fight the oligarchy.” [Sen. Bernie Sanders] You know, I used to talk about oligarchy and people’d say, “What is he talking about?” Everybody knows what I'm talking about tonight."],[130,"[Faiz Shakir] At the same time, Zohran Mamdani was polling at all of 1% in New York. But of course, that would soon change. [Zohran Mamdani] Tonight you have delivered a mandate for change, a mandate for a new kind of politics, a mandate for a city we can afford, and a mandate for a government that delivers exactly that. [Faiz Shakir] What Zohran Mamdani’s amazing campaign in New York showed is how to win working-class people across the spectrum, even as he was derided by big-moneyed interests and many of the media elite as being a far-left agenda."],[169,"[Fox News host] And I'm sure Republicans look at what Zohran Mamdani just said yesterday and say, please say more of that, because that does give us an opening in the midterm elections. [Faiz Shakir] Those who were paying attention keenly were taking notes, and they were changing the way that they were talking. James Carville, by late November, is saying that economic populism needs to be the message of all Democrats. And the campaigns started to change, too."],[193,"[James Talarico] The only minority destroying America is the billionaires. [Faiz Shakir] This chart of ad spending on issue by issue is a good shorthand for how much Democrats centered affordability and economic populism this year. Two years ago, the top ad issues for Democrats looked very different, with Trump's character among the top five issues for both Senate and House race ad buys."],[218,"That economic prism of talking about class-based issues pervaded all Democratic campaigns. Gallons of gas, gallons of milk. Trump and Rogers could care less how much these things cost. I am so tired of working people being told that we should settle for scraps while the richest people in this country get permanent relief. That is all backwards. Across Alaska, we are getting crushed by corporate greed."],[241,"The biggest corporations and the richest Americans have grabbed unimaginable wealth at your expense. In my view, economic populism is defined by a few core things. First, you have to be willing to take on people with power. To drive private equity out of housing, health care, nursing homes. Name the villain. We are all being taken advantage of by Big Tech, by these data centers."],[264,"I'm Dr. Annie Andrews. I'll go after big insurance companies overcharging you and ripping us off. When Big Pharma raised your bills, I took them on. Who are we up against? Who is depriving us of economic power? Elon Musk wants our land. He wants our water. He wants our tax dollars. And he wants his very own personal United States senator. Second: what specific agenda items do you want to put on the docket to improve the lives of working-class Americans?"],[293,"— Money out of? — Politics! — Money in your? — Pocket! — Medicare for? — All! That's right. Ban them from denying care a doctor says you need. I want to expand Medicare to cover vision, dental and hearing. Stopping these stupid wars around the world so that we can bring our money and resources home and invest in housing we can all afford, health care we can count on and Social Security."],[315,"And third: how are you building a grassroots movement that reflects the emotions of the working-class people, their anger, their frustrations? In this election cycle, Republicans largely hid from public view. When there were town halls, he walked out of that. So you're not actually listening and hearing people's pain. [Faiz] Abdul El-Sayed held over 700 public events in Michigan alone. [Adam Hamilton] If any of you were angry and upset, I was going to listen to that, too."],[343,"And I've had church people angry and upset with me. I don't walk out of the room when people are angry or upset. James Talarico did hundreds of events in Texas. So, you stay here, you answer our questions, or you suffer the consequences. I appreciate you being here and I appreciate you traveling in and I appreciate... I did it for my people, not for you. And I think that’s wonderful. It’s all right. It’s all right. It’s all right. This is— this is what this conversation is supposed to be about."],[368,"This is how Democrats won, by talking to working-class people, hearing their pain, anger and frustration, and channeling that towards an economic agenda to improve their lives. One cautionary note about the Election Day outcomes is that while individual Democratic candidates did well, the Democratic Party brand is still suffering, with majorities disapproving of it. Democratic Party leadership did not come forward with a specific agenda to offer working-class people in this election cycle."],[399,"It was left to individual candidates themselves to form agendas, to speak to the working-class people of their states. The opportunity now is to present an agenda that speaks for a Democratic Party writ large. And it's not going to come from the Democratic leadership that we have. Here are five things Democrats should do if they want to remain the party of the working class. These agenda items, mind you, are wildly popular in Texas, Georgia, Kansas, Michigan and everywhere else the Democrats won on election night."],[430,"First, end the wars. If we're going to be serious about ending the wars, we need to leverage ending the funding for those wars. Second, raise the cap on taxable income on Social Security. Make billionaires pay their fair share so that we can expand Social Security benefits for working-class Americans. Third, raise the minimum wage to a living wage. Fourth, break up big medicine's corporate monopolies and provide better health care for more people."],[457,"And fifth, rein in the power of the Big Tech oligarchs, protect communities from unchecked data center development and create new AI safety guardrails. We sent a crystal-clear message to the people at the top. We will not be conquered. Michigan, we did it! I think we just made some history. [Faiz] Let's be clear. The biggest overriding issue of this election cycle was Donald Trump's corruption and his lack of action on anything to improve working-class people's lives."],[491,"In order for economic populists to win against this backdrop, you had to provide a sense that you were focused on economic issues. And against a media discourse that is often pitting identity politics to distract one candidate or another, we saw across the board, candidates focused on talking about health care, talking about the economy, talking about AI and data center development."],[516,"They were doing so in ways that were focused and attentive to economic pain and suffering. They may have talked about those issues in slightly different ways. Not all candidates were for Medicare for all, but all candidates were talking about health care expansion. Not all candidates were for taxing the rich in specific ways, but all candidates were for raising the tax rates on the wealthiest in society."],[538,"Discussing economic justice issues and being focused on economic populism while Donald Trump had nothing to offer the working-class people of this country provided the path to win enormous victories. Don"]],"paras":true}};
})(window.MOSAIC);
